hadiths[605]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: What do you think, if I dip my hands into a kizamah (a narrow water vessel) with a single dip? He said: It suffices you, and the foot is the same, but clean it thoroughly."
"2","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: (About) ""Wash your faces and your hands up to the elbows"" - is it part of what is washed? He said: Yes, there is no doubt about that."
"3","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ziyad informed me that Fulayh ibn Sulayman informed him that Abu Hurayrah performed ablution and washed the rufghayn (the folds at the upper arms). It was said to him: What do you intend by this? He said: I want to perfect my tahjil (the brightness of my ablution limbs)."
"4","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Yahya ibn Umarah ibn Abi Hasan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe his head once with his palms, moving his hands forward and backward over his head, one single time."
"5","From Malik, from Amr ibn Yahya, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zayd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped his head with his hands, bringing them forward and taking them back, beginning with the front of his head, then returning them to the place from which he began."
"6","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Nafi informed me that Ibn Umar used to place the inside of his right palm on the water, then he would not shake it off, then wipe with it what is between his horn (side of head) to his forehead one time, not adding to it."
"7","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar used to put his hands into the ablution water and wipe with them a single wiping over the crown of the head only."
"8","From al-Thawri, from Abd Rabbihi, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he used to wipe his head once."
"9","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from al-Kalbi, from al-Asbagh ibn Nubatah, from Ali, that he performed ablution and wiped his head a single wiping."
"10","From Israil, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah, he said: I heard Mujahid say: Even if I were on the bank of the Euphrates, I would not wipe my head more than once."
"11","From Mamar, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi bint Afra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped his head twice. He said: And it reached me that Ali said: He wiped three times."
"12","From Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Amir, he said: I saw Ali perform ablution, then he took a handful of water and placed it on his head, and I saw it running down over all sides of his head."
"13","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: The most I wipe my head is three times, no more and no less, with a single handful, without considering it obligatory."
"14","From al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, he said: If one wipes part of his head, it suffices him."
"15","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: How does one with two braids wipe his head? He said: Only over what lies on his head of them, and he should not shave his head, nor wipe merely the ends of the hair. Then Ata placed his hand on his head and wiped the hair at its roots, passing his palms over what was on his head, pouring out his palms, and he did not bring them back upward against the hair. And I saw him, and he did not repeat (the wiping of) the head. And I asked him about one with a thick mass of hair? He said: This same ruling applies to both. And I saw Ubayd ibn Umayr, and he had a thick mass of hair, and he would hold back what fell over his face, doing so between his ears and his head, and he would touch only that which he placed between his ears and his head, and he would not touch of his mass of hair except what was on his head only."
"16","From al-Thawri, he said: If a man wipes his head and does not wipe his ears, it suffices him; but if he wipes his ears and does not wipe his head, it does not suffice him."
"17","From Mamar, he said: One who heard al-Hasan say informed me: It suffices you to wipe your head with what remains on your hands from the ablution water."
"18","From Israil, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, he said: I heard Musab ibn Sad, and a man asked him: I perform ablution, washing my face and forearms - does what remains on my hands suffice for my head, or should I take fresh water for my head? He said: No, rather take fresh water for your head."
"19","Mamar informed us, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar used to take fresh water for his head. He said: Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, the same."
"20","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Ajlan informed us that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe his ears along with his face once, and wipe his head, dipping his palms in the water, then wiping with them the front of his head, the crown, then the back of the head, then the temples, then wiping his ears a single wiping - all of that with what was in his palm from that single taking of water."
"21","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: Do you wipe your head with the leftover water of your face? He said: No, but I dip my hands in the water and wipe with them, and I do not shake them off, nor wait for what is in them of water to dry, and I am keen to wet the hair."
"22","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The ears are part of the head."
"23","From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The ears are part of the head. From al-Thawri, from Abu al-Nadr, from Said ibn Marjanah, from Ibn Umar, the same."
"24","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Nafi informed me that Ibn Umar used to wash the backs and insides of his ears except the earhole, along with the face, once or twice, and after wiping his head he would put his fingers into the water, then insert them into the earholes once. And he said: I saw him when he was dying - he performed ablution, then put his fingers in the water and tried to insert them into his earholes but they would not find the way, and he did not stop until I myself put my finger in the water and inserted them into his earholes."
"25","From Abdullah ibn Muharrar, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The ears are part of the head."
"26","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, he said: We used to perform ablution for Ibn Umar when he was ill, and he would order us to wipe his ears along with what he wiped. He said: And Ayyub informed me, from Nafi, he said: Once we forgot to wipe his ears, and he kept bringing his hands near his ears but could not reach them, and we did not know what he wanted, until later we realized it and wiped them, and then he became calm."
"27","From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar, when he performed ablution, used to wipe his ears along with his head, putting his fingers in the water and wiping his ears with them, then turning his thumbs behind his ears."
"28","Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar used to put his hands into the ablution water and wipe with them a single wiping over the crown only, then put his fingers in the water, then insert them into his ears, then turn his thumbs behind his ears."
"29","From Mamar, from Qatadah, that he used to wipe the two ears and say: The ears are part of the head."
"30","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, that he used to wipe the backs and insides of the ears."
"31","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: Follow with your fingers the insides of the ears, washing them with the leftover water of your face each time you scoop water over your face. I said: What if I delay wiping them until I wipe them along with the head? He said: It will not harm you."
"32","From Israil, from Amir, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Uthman, that he performed ablution and wiped his ears, their outer and inner sides, and said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing it."
"33","From Mamar, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi bint Afra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped his ears, their outer and inner sides."
"34","From al-Thawri, from Mutarrif, from al-Shabi, he said: Whatever of the ears faces the face is part of the face - he says: he washes it - and their outer side is part of the head."
"35","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Husayn ibn Abdullah ibn Ubaydullah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The ears are neither part of the face nor part of the head. Had they been part of the head, the hair on them would have to be shaved, and had they been part of the face, their backs and insides would have to be washed along with the face."
"36","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: From where do you consider the ears (to be)? He said: Part of the head. He said: And I wipe them along with the face each time I pour water over my face. I said: Is it binding on me to remove the dirt of the ears? He said: No."
"37","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: How does a bald man wipe? He said: He wipes his whole head, what has hair on it and what is bald of it - the water reaches what it reaches and misses what it misses, and he is not required to clean it thoroughly."
"38","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, he was asked about a man who forgot to wipe his head until he prayed. He said: If he wishes, he repeats the ablution and the prayer."
"39","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: If you forget the wiping of the head and pray, then remember, then wipe your head and repeat the prayer. He said: And it reached me from him - and I am not sure I heard it - he says: If there is wetness in your beard, then wipe from it."
"40","From Mamar, from Amr, from al-Hasan, about one who forgets the wiping of the head in ablution, he said: If there is wetness in his beard, let him wipe his head with it only, and repeat the prayer."
"41","From al-Thawri, he said: If one forgets the wiping, he wipes and repeats the prayer, but does not repeat the ablution. And if he forgets the wiping and rain falls on his head, that suffices him - it is purification."
"42","From Mamar, from Qatadah, about a man who forgets to sniff water into the nose, or wipe his ears, or rinse his mouth, until he enters the prayer and then remembers - he does not leave (the prayer) for that. He said: But if he forgot to wipe his head and remembers while in prayer, he leaves and wipes his head."
"43","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: If one forgets the wiping of the head, he repeats the prayer."
"44","From al-Thawri, about a man who forgets the wiping of his head, then stands and says the takbir in prayer, then laughs - he said: He leaves and wipes his head and does not repeat the ablution, because his prayer was not (valid), nor was his ablution complete."
"45","From Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, he said: If you forget the wiping of the head and find wetness in your beard, wipe your head with it. From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, and al-Thawri, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, the same. Al-Thawri said: And others preferred (using) water other than it. Sufyan said: I think it was Musab ibn Sad."
"46","From Israil ibn Yunus, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, he said: I heard Musab ibn Sad, and a man asked him: I perform ablution, washing my face and forearms - does what is on my hands suffice for the head, or should I take fresh water for my head? He said: Rather, take fresh water for your head."
"47","From Mamar, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, he said: I asked Ibn al-Musayyib: How does a woman wipe her head? He said: She removes her head-covering, then wipes her head."
"48","From Malik, from Nafi, he said: I saw Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd perform ablution when I was a boy, and when she wanted to wipe her head, she removed the head-covering."
"49","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: She wipes over her clothes at the beginning of the day, and touches the water to the ends of the hair of her forelock from the direction of the forehead."
"50","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah and al-Hasan, they said about this verse: ""O you who believe, when you stand for prayer, wash your faces and your hands up to the elbows, and wipe your heads and your feet up to the ankles"" - they said: The two feet are wiped."
"51","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Yazid, or Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Allah made obligatory two washings and two wipings. Do you not see that He mentioned dry ablution (tayammum), making two wipings in place of the two washings, and leaving the two wipings? And a man said to Matar al-Warraq: Who used to say wiping over the feet? He said: Many jurists."
"52","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that he heard Ikrimah say: Ibn Abbas said: Ablution is two wipings and two washings."
"53","From Ibn Uyaynah, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from al-Shabi, he said: As for Gabriel (peace be upon him), he indeed came down with (the ruling of) wiping over the feet."
"54","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Abu al-Sawda, he said: I heard Ibn Abd Khayr narrate from his father, he said: I saw Ali perform ablution, and he began washing the tops of his feet, and said: Were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washing the tops of his feet, I would have considered the soles of the feet more deserving of washing than their tops."
"55","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: Why do I not wipe the feet as I wipe the head, when both were mentioned together? He said: I do not see but that he wiped the head and washed the feet. I heard Abu Hurayrah say: Woe to the heels from the Fire. Ata said: Some people say it is wiping, but as for me, I wash them."
"56","From Mamar, from Qatadah, that Ibn Masud said: He returned to the washing of the feet in His saying: ""and your feet up to the ankles""."
"57","From Mamar, from Hisham ibn Urwah, that his father said: The wiping over the feet returned to washing in His saying: ""and your feet up to the ankles""."
"58","From Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Uthman ibn Abi Suwayd, that he mentioned to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz the wiping over the feet, and he said: It has reached me from three of the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the lowest of them your cousin al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washed his feet."
"59","Mamar informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I saw Abu Hurayrah pass by people performing ablution from the water vessel, and he said: Perfect your ablution, may Allah have mercy on you. Have you not heard what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"60","Mamar informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"61","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from a man, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked down upon us while we were performing ablution, and said: Woe to the heels from the Fire. He said: So we set about washing them thoroughly and rubbing them."
"62","From Mamar, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washed his feet three times each. Then she said to us: Ibn Abbas came to me and asked me about this hadith, and I informed him, and he said: People insist on nothing but washing, while we find in the Book of Allah the Exalted the wiping - meaning the feet."
"63","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: When you scoop water with both your hands over your feet, wash the hand with which you wash the soles of your feet before putting it into the water."
"64","From Mamar, from Amr, from al-Hasan, he used to say: Run water between your fingers before Allah runs (them) with the Fire."
"65","From al-Thawri, from Abu Miskin, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from Ibn Masud, he said: A man will surely clean thoroughly between his fingers in ablution, or the Fire will surely clean him."
"66","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Said ibn Abi Said, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr performed ablution in the presence of Aishah, and she said to him: Perfect the ablution, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"67","From Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he washed his feet, used to run (water) between his toes."
"68","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Talhah ibn Musarrif and Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, they said: Run (water) between the fingers, lest Allah stuff them with fire."
"69","From Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that Abu Bakr used to run (water) between his fingers when he performed ablution."
"70","From Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar in his ablution used to clean his feet thoroughly, and clean the fingers of his hands along with the toes of his feet, following that up until he cleaned them."
"71","From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar used to run (water) between his fingers when he performed ablution."
"72","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Yahya ibn Said informed me, from Muhammad ibn Mahmud, that it reached him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at a blind man performing ablution, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began saying: The soles of the feet - but the blind man could not hear him - and the blind man began washing the soles of the feet, and so he was named al-Basir (the seeing one)."
"73","From Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar used to wash his feet with most of his ablution. Abd al-Razzaq said: And I myself performed ablution for al-Thawri, and I saw him do that - washing them abundantly."
"74","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Yahya ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Mahmud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at a man blind of sight performing ablution, while he was at a distance from him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Little (washed are) the soles of the feet. So he washed the soles of the feet, and he was named al-Basir."
"75","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: About His saying ""and your feet up to the ankles"" - do you consider the ankles part of what is washed of the feet? He said: Yes, there is no doubt about it."
"76","From al-Thawri, from Ismail ibn Kathir, from Asim ibn Laqit ibn Sabirah, from his father, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned some things, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perfect the ablution, run (water) between the fingers, and when you sniff water into the nose, do it thoroughly, unless you are fasting."
"77","He said: I am Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ismail ibn Kathir Abu Hashim al-Makki narrated to us, from Asim ibn Laqit ibn Sabirah, from his father or his grandfather, he said: I set out with some companions of mine until we reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but did not find him. Aishah fed us dates and prepared porridge for us, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came walking briskly. He said: Has she fed you anything? We said: Yes. While we were thus, the shepherd drove the sheep into the pen, with a kid in his hand. He said: Has it given birth? He said: Yes. He said: Then slaughter a sheep for them. Then he turned to us and said: Do not think - and he did not say do not deem - that we slaughtered the sheep for your sake; we have a hundred sheep and do not want them to increase - when the shepherd delivers a lamb for us, we order him and he slaughters a sheep. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about ablution. He said: When you perform ablution, perfect it, run (water) between the fingers, and when you sniff water, do it thoroughly, unless you are fasting. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a wife - and he mentioned her long tongue and foul speech - and he said: Divorce her. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, she has companionship and children. He said: Keep her and admonish her; if there is good in her she will comply, and do not beat your traveling companion (wife) as you beat your slave-girl."
"78","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: If you dip your hand in a kizamah (narrow vessel), clean it and that suffices you, and do not begin with your left foot before your right."
"79","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, about a man who puts his feet into a river without touching them with his hand, he said: It suffices him."
"80","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: What if a person performs ablution then steps on dung - is he still in ablution? He said: No, but let him wash the dung off and clean it. He said: And I say: Take this - and if he steps on manure, let him rub his feet on the ground - or he said: on the dust. From Israil, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Ibrahim, the same as the saying of al-Shabi."
"81","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: If a man steps with filth of a human up to the ankles, he need only wash his feet."
"82","From Mamar, from Qatadah, about a man whose body is soiled with urine or blood while he is in ablution, he said: He washes off the trace of urine and blood, and does not perform ablution anew."
"83","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from Ata and Tawus, and from (other) men, they said: If you step on moist filth, wash it; if it is dry, there is no harm."
"84","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: What if I step on dry dung - do I wash the soles of my feet? He said: No. I said: What about my hands and face, if something of that dry dung touches them? He said: No. By my life, when we walk with a funeral, the wind blows dry dung over our faces, yet we do not perform ablution nor wash our faces nor anything of that."
"85","From Mamar, from Asim ibn Sulayman, he said: We used to visit Abu al-Aliyah al-Riyahi and perform ablution, and he would say: Do you not perform ablution in your lodgings? We would say: Yes, but we step in filth. He said: No ablution is due on you. Shall I not tell you of something worse than that - the wind blows it onto your heads and beards."
"86","From Mamar, from Hammad, he said: If a man steps on dry dung, no ablution is due on him; and if he touches a dog, no ablution is due on him."
"87","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: If that (filth) touches my garment, should I sprinkle it? He said: No."
"88","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: We went out one day with Ibn al-Musayyib to a mosque, and the ground had been rained upon and there was mud. When we reached the door of the mosque, a man of the company washed his feet, and Ibn al-Musayyib said to him: Had you not performed ablution in your lodging? He said: Yes, but we walked through this mud. He said: No ablution is due on you."
"89","From Mamar, he said: One who saw al-Hasan walking in mud informed me, he said: The mud did not reach the tops of the feet, but it filled their soles. When he reached the door of the mosque, he wiped the soles of his feet on the ground, then entered the mosque without washing them."
"90","From Mamar, from Qatadah, about a man whose body is soiled with urine and blood while he is in ablution, he said: He washes off the trace of blood and urine, and does not perform ablution anew."
"91","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, he said: I saw Ibn Umar at Mina perform ablution, then go out barefoot, stepping on whatever he stepped on, then enter the mosque and pray without performing ablution."
"92","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, he said: Alqamah and al-Aswad used to wade through water and mud in the rain, then enter the mosque and pray."
"93","From al-Thawri, from Yahya ibn al-Ala, from al-Amash, he said: I saw Yahya ibn Waththab, Abdullah ibn Ayyash, and others of the companions of Abdullah wading through water mixed with manure and urine, and when they reached the door of the mosque, they did no more than shake off their feet, then entered the prayer."
"94","From Yahya ibn al-Ala, from al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, he said: A man asked Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr about the mud of rain, and he said: You ask me about two purifiers together. Allah said: ""And We sent down blessed water from the sky,"" and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The earth has been made for me a mosque and a purifier."
"95","From al-Thawri, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Alqamah ibn Qays, he said: Ablution is for (ritual) impurity, not for treading (on things)."
"96","From al-Thawri, from Abu Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Ablution is for what comes out, not for what goes in, and no ablution is due for treading (on something)."
"97","From Ibn Uyaynah, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud, he said: We used not to perform ablution for treading (on something)."
"98","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was informed from Muslim ibn Abi Imran that Ibn Masud said: We used not to perform ablution for treading, nor uncover a covering, nor gather up hair. He said: His saying ""nor uncover a covering"" means his hand when a garment is over it in prayer."
"99","From Bishr ibn Rafi, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Masud, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to uncover a covering, gather up hair, or renew ablution. He said: I said to Yahya: His saying ""or renew ablution"" - he said: When one steps on filth while in ablution. And his saying ""nor uncover a covering"" means: he does not uncover the garment from his hand when he prostrates."
"100","From Abdullah ibn Ziyad ibn Saman, he said: al-Qaqa ibn Hakim informed me, from Aishah, she said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man who steps with his sandals on filth. He said: Dust is a purifier for them."
"101","From Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from a woman of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we have a foul-smelling road in the rain. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is there not a clean road short of it? I said: Yes. He said: Then that is for that."
"102","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Ajlan, from Said ibn Abi Said, that a woman asked Aishah about a woman who drags her train when she goes out to the mosque and it touches an impure place. She said: Then she passes over a clean place, and it purifies it."
"103","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Abu Raja al-Utaridi, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas on this pulpit on a rainy Friday saying: Pray in your lodgings, and do not bring filth transferring it with your feet to the mosque, for not every jar of the mosque suffices for your purification."
"104","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: Water is carried with me on a rainy day until I come to the door of the mosque, and I wash them (my feet) there."
"105","From al-Thawri, about a man who performs ablution, then his foot plunges into filth and he finds no water, he said: He performs dry ablution (tayammum) - is he like a man who did not complete his ablution? He said: If something (filth) touches any of the ablution or tayammum limbs, he wipes it with dust, and it stands in place of water."
"106","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: A man asked Ata, he said: I asked: I touched my sandal in prayer and my hand fell on filth - do I repeat my prayer? He said: No."
"107","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from Amir al-Shabi, about a man who prayed with filth in his leather socks, he said: He repeats."
"108","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: One of my feet missed or I forgot it until I remembered later, and I did nothing (breaking) in between. He said: Wash what you missed, and do not start a fresh ablution anew."
"109","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: I forgot a small part of the ablution limbs of the body. He said: Then touch it with water."
"110","From Mamar, from Amr ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, he said: Whoever forgets something of his limbs in ablution, let him not repeat the ablution, whether the ablution has dried or not; let him wash what he left, and repeat the prayer."
"111","From Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Sabrah, from Yahya ibn Said, from Ibn al-Musayyib, he said: Whoever leaves anything of the ablution places, let him repeat - let him wash what he left, then repeat the prayer, even if it is like (a spot the size of) a hair."
"112","From Hushaym ibn Bashir, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, he said: I heard Ibrahim al-Nakhai say: Whatever the water reaches of the purification places, that place is purified."
"113","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: Whoever forgets something of his ablution limbs, if his ablution has not dried, let him wash what he left; but if it has dried, he repeats the ablution and the prayer in its time."
"114","From Mamar, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, that Umar ibn al-Khattab saw a man praying who had left a spot the size of a fingernail on his foot, and ordered him to repeat the ablution and the prayer."
"115","Mamar informed us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib, he said: I visited al-Rubayyi bint Afra, and she said: Who are you? He said: I said: I am Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib. She said: Who is your mother? I said: Raytah bint Ali, or so-and-so bint Ali ibn Abi Talib. She said: Welcome, O son of my sister. I said: I have come to ask you about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to join us and visit us, and he used to perform ablution in this vessel or one like it, about a mudd. She said: He would wash his hands, rinse his mouth and sniff water into his nose, then wash his face three times, then wash his hands three times each, then wipe his head twice, wipe his ears their outer and inner sides, and wash his feet three times. Then she said: Ibn Abbas visited me and asked me about this hadith, and I informed him, and he said: People insist on nothing but washing, while we find in the Book of Allah the wiping over the feet."
"116","I am al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayyah ibn Qays, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he performed ablution three times (each limb), then wiped his head, then drank the leftover of his ablution water, then said: Whoever wishes to look at the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), let him look at this."
"117","Israil ibn Yunus informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayyah ibn Qays, from Ali, he said: I witnessed Ali in al-Rahbah urinate, then perform ablution, washing his palms three times, rinsing and sniffing three times, washing his face three times and his forearms three times each, wiping his head, washing his feet three times, then drawing (water) standing, then taking and drinking the leftover of his ablution water. Then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do as you have seen me do, so I wanted to show you."
"118","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd al-Karim informed me, from al-Kharifi, that Ali in Kufa said to his servant: O Qunbur, bring me ablution water. He brought it to him. Al-Mughirah, from Abd al-Karim, (said): In a large cup - so he began and washed his hands before putting them into the ablution water three times, then rinsed three times and sniffed three times, then washed his face three times, then washed his right hand up to the elbow three times, then the left likewise, then scooped a handful of water with one hand onto his head and wiped with it - he said: in summer, as if he scooped it for the summer - he said: then washed his right foot up to the ankles three times, then the left likewise, then stood up and drank from the leftover of his ablution water. Then he said: Whoever loves to look at the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), let him perform ablution thus. He said: And they hold that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank the leftover of his ablution water standing, as Ali did, then prayed the prescribed prayer. He said: Then he did not leave his seat until he called Qunbur for the ablution water of prayer, then scooped a single handful and rinsed and sniffed from it, and wiped his face, forearms, head and feet from that handful, a single wiping for each limb, dividing it - rinsing and sniffing, wiping his face, forearms and head once - then he said: Such is the ablution of one who has not broken it - he says: if he wishes to perform ablution, and if he wishes, not."
"119","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: One whom I trust informed me that Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Husayn informed him, he said: My father informed me, from his father, he said: Ali called for ablution water and it was brought near to him. He washed his palms three times before putting them into his ablution water, then rinsed three times and sniffed three times, then washed his face three times, then washed his right hand up to the elbow three times, then the left likewise, then wiped his head a single wiping, then washed his right foot up to the ankles three times, then the left likewise, then stood up and said to me: Hand me (the vessel). So I handed him the vessel containing the leftover of his ablution water, and he drank from the leftover of his ablution water standing, and I was amazed. When he saw my amazement, he said: Do not be amazed, for I saw your father, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), do as you have seen me do - he means: with this ablution of his, and drinking the leftover of his ablution water standing."
"120","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata informed me that it reached him from Uthman ibn Affan that he rinsed three times and sniffed three times, then poured over his face three times, and over his hands three times, then washed his feet three times each, then said: Thus did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution. He said: And I did not verify it from Uthman; I neither added to it nor omitted."
"121","From Israil, from Amir ibn Shaqiq, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, he said: I saw Uthman ibn Affan perform ablution: he washed his palms three times each, rinsed, sniffed and blew out, washed his face three times - he said: and I think he said: and his forearms three times each - then wiped his head and his ears, their outer and inner sides, washed his feet three times each, ran (water) between his fingers, and ran (water) through his beard when he washed his face, before washing his feet. Then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do as you have seen me do."
"122","Mamar informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that he performed ablution washing each limb once, then mentioned that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do it."
"123","From Dawud ibn Qays, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution once each (limb)."
"124","From al-Thawri, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: Shall I not inform you of the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he scooped with his right hand, then poured onto the left, pour by pour."
"125","From Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution two (kinds of) ablution: once and thrice."
"126","From Dawud ibn Qays, from Ubaydullah ibn Miqsam, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, that he was asked about three handfuls in ablution, and he said: Whoever knows how to perform ablution well, one handful suffices him."
"127","From al-Thawri, from Yahya ibn Said, from a man, from Ibn Abbas, that he performed ablution once."
"128","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, he said: Once suffices when one perfects the ablution."
"129","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: If a man performed ablution once, doing it thoroughly in that single time, it suffices him."
"130","From al-Thawri, from Abdullah ibn Jabir, from Jabir, from al-Hasan, he said: Once suffices, and twice suffices."
"131","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: One who saw Umar ibn al-Khattab perform ablution twice informed me."
"132","From Mamar, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, that he saw Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, perform ablution twice (each limb)."
"133","From al-Thawri, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Mujahid, he said: I used to pour ablution water for Ibn Umar, sometimes twice and sometimes thrice."
"134","From Malik ibn Anas, from Amr ibn Yahya al-Mazini, that a man said to Abdullah ibn Zayd, who was of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Can you show me how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution? He said: Yes. So Abdullah ibn Zayd called for ablution water, poured over his hands and washed them twice, then rinsed and sniffed thrice, washed his face thrice, then washed his hands up to the elbows twice, then wiped his head with his hands, bringing them forward and back, beginning with the front of his head, then going with them to his nape, then returning them to the place from which he began, then washed his feet."
"135","Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Humran ibn Aban, he said: I saw Uthman ibn Affan perform ablution: he poured over his hands thrice and washed them, then rinsed and sniffed, then washed his face thrice, then washed his right hand up to the elbow thrice, then the left the same, then wiped his head, then washed his right foot thrice, then the left thrice likewise. Then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution like my ablution. Then he said: Whoever performs ablution like this ablution of mine, then prays two rakahs without conversing with himself in them, is forgiven his past sins."
"136","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to him, from Ata ibn Zayd al-Jundai, that he heard Humran, freedman of Uthman, that Uthman performed ablution: he poured over his hands three times, sniffed thrice, rinsed thrice, washed his face thrice, washed his right hand up to the elbow thrice, and the left the same, then wiped his head, then washed his right foot thrice, then the left the same. Then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution like my ablution. Then he said: Whoever performs ablution like this ablution of mine, then stands and bows two rakahs without conversing with himself in them, is forgiven his past sins."
"137","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Humran, freedman of Uthman, he said: Uthman sat at the sitting places and called for ablution water and performed ablution, then said: By Allah, I shall narrate to you a hadith - were it not for a verse in the Book of Allah, I would not have narrated it to you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No man performs ablution perfecting it, but he is forgiven what is between it and the next prayer, until he prays it. He said: I heard it from him."
"138","From Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Ata, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, taking turns grazing the camels. One day I came while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering a sermon, and some of his speech had preceded me, so I sat beside Umar ibn al-Khattab. I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever performs ablution perfecting it, then stands and prays, praying a prayer knowing what he says in it until he finishes his prayer, is like his state the day his mother bore him. He said: I said: Excellent, excellent. Umar ibn al-Khattab said: He said just now something better than this. He said: Whoever performs ablution perfecting it, then stands and prays a prayer knowing what he says in it until he finishes his prayer, then says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, eight gates of Paradise are opened for him, entering through whichever he wishes."
"139","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, that Abu Musa al-Ashari said: We kindle (sins) against ourselves, then when we pray the prescribed prayer, the prayer expiates what came before it. Then we kindle against ourselves, then when we pray, the prayer expiates what came before it."
"140","From Mamar, from Aban, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: Salman al-Farisi said: When the believing servant stands for prayer, his sins are placed on his head, and he does not finish his prayer until they scatter from him, as the date-clusters of the palm scatter, falling right and left."
"141","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Misar, from Zayd al-Ammi, from al-Hasan, he said: No caller of the people of the earth calls to prayer until a caller of the people of heaven calls: Stand, O children of Adam, and extinguish your fires. He said: So the caller to prayer stands and calls, then the people stand for prayer."
"142","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Misar, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Kathir al-Zubaydi, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: There came out on the neck of Adam a shaafah, meaning a blister. He prayed a prayer and it descended to his chest, then prayed a prayer and it descended to the waist, then prayed a prayer and it descended to the palm, then prayed a prayer and it descended to the thumb, then prayed a prayer and it went away."
"143","From al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud said: The prayers are expiations for what is between them, so long as major sins are avoided."
"144","Al-Thawri informed us, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubayl, from Tariq ibn Shihab, that he spent the night with Salman to observe his striving. He said: He stood and prayed at the end of the night, and it was as if he did not see what he had expected. He mentioned that to him, and Salman said: Guard these five prayers, for they are expiations for these wounds, so long as the mortal blow (major sin) is not struck. When evening comes, people are in three stations: among them one who has (reward) and nothing against him, among them one who has (sin) against him and nothing for him, and among them one with neither for him nor against him. A man seizes the darkness of night and the heedlessness of people, and stands praying until morning - that is for him and nothing against him. A man seizes the heedlessness of people and the darkness of night, and plunges headlong into sins - that is against him and nothing for him. And a man prays Isha, then sleeps - that is neither for him nor against him. So beware of overexertion (haqhaqah), and upon you is moderation and constancy."
"145","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Salih, freedman of al-Tawamah, from al-Saib ibn Khabbab, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: A man's prayer in his house is light, and when a man stands for prayer, his sins are hung above him, and he does not prostrate a prostration but Allah expiates thereby a sin from him."
"146","From Ibn Uyaynah, from a man of Basra, from al-Hasan, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The one praying has three qualities: mercy showers upon him from his feet to the expanse of the sky, angels gather around him from his head to the reaches of the sky, and a caller calls out: if the one in intimate prayer knew whom he converses with, he would never turn away."""
"147","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata' said to me: When he rinses his mouth, what comes out of his mouth are sins, and when he blows his nose, what comes out of his nose are sins, and when he washes his face, what comes out of it are sins, and when he washes his hands, what falls from them are sins, and when he wipes his head, what falls from it of impurities are sins, and when he washes his feet, what falls from them are sins, until he returns as his mother bore him, except for major sins."
"148","From al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from al-Qasim al-Shami: that a freedwoman of his called Umm Hashim seated him behind a screen with ink and pen, and sent for Abu Umamah, and asked him about a hadith he had narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about ablution. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever stands for ablution and washes his hands, sins come out of his hands; when he rinses his mouth, sins come out of his mouth; when he blows his nose, they come out of his nose, and likewise until he washes the feet. Then if he goes out to an obligatory prayer, it is like an accepted Hajj, and if he goes out to a voluntary prayer, it is like an accepted Umrah."""
"149","From Muqatil, and a man, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which part of the night is best? He said: The last middle of the night. He said: Then prayer is accepted until the Fajr prayer, then there is no prayer until the sun rises, then prayer is accepted until the Asr prayer, then there is no prayer until the sun sets. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how is the night prayer? He said: ""Two by two."" He said: I said: How is the day prayer? He said: ""Four by four."" He said: ""And whoever sends blessings upon me once, Allah writes for him a qirat, and a qirat is like Uhud. And when a servant stands to perform ablution and washes his palms, his sins come out of his palms, then when he rinses his mouth and sniffs water, his sins come out of his nostrils, then when he washes his face, his sins come out of his face, hearing and sight, then when he washes his forearms, his sins come out of his forearms, then when he wipes his head, his sins come out of his head, then when he washes his feet, his sins come out of his feet, then when he stands for prayer, he comes out of his sins as on the day his mother bore him."""
"150","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Amr ibn Abasah, who said: He was sitting with some companions when a man said to him: Who will narrate to us a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Amr said: I will. He said: Go on, by Allah, and be careful. He said: I heard him say: ""Whoever grows a grey hair in the way of Allah, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection."" He said: Go on, by Allah, and be careful."
"151","He said: And I heard him say: ""Whoever shoots an arrow in the way of Allah, it will equal (the freeing of) a slave."" He said: Go on, by Allah, and be careful."
"152","He said: And I heard him say: ""Whoever frees a soul, Allah will free, for every limb of it, a limb of him from the Fire."""
"153","He said: And I heard him say: ""Whoever frees two souls, Allah will free, for every two limbs of them, two limbs of him from the Fire."" He said: Go on, by Allah, and be careful."
"154","He said: And (I heard) a hadith which, had I heard it from him only once or twice or three or four or five times, I would not have narrated it to you: There is no Muslim servant who performs ablution and washes his face but the sins of his face fall from the edges of his beard; when he washes his hands, the sins of his hands fall from between his nails; when he wipes his head, the sins of his head fall from the ends of his hair; when he washes his feet, the sins of his feet fall from their soles. Then if he comes to a mosque and prays in congregation in it, his reward falls upon Allah; and if he stands and prays two rak'ahs, they will be an expiation. He said: Go on, by Allah, and be careful; narrate and do not err."
"155","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When the servant rinses his mouth, every sin he spoke with comes out with the water as it leaves his mouth; when he washes his face, every sin on his face comes out with the water dripping from his face; when he washes his hands, sins come out of his hands with the water dripping from his hands; and when he washes his feet, sins come out of his feet as he washes them. Then when he leaves his house for the mosque, a sin is erased for every step and a good deed added, until he enters the mosque."
"156","From Qays ibn al-Rabi', from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Tha'labah ibn Abbad, from his father, who said: I do not know how many times he narrated this hadith to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There is no servant who performs ablution and perfects it until water flows over his face, then washes his forearms until water flows over his elbows, then washes his feet until water flows from his heels, then prays and perfects his prayer, but he is forgiven what has passed."
"157","From al-Thawri, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution for every prayer, until the day of the Conquest, when he prayed Zuhr, Asr and Maghrib with a single ablution."
"158","Al-Thawri reported to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the prayers with a single ablution and wiped over his leather socks. Umar said to him: O Messenger of Allah! You did something you never used to do? He said: ""I did it deliberately, O Umar!"""
"159","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Yunus ibn Jubayr Abu Ghallab, from Hittan ibn Abdillah al-Raqashi, who said: We were with Abu Musa al-Ash'ari in an army on the bank of the Tigris when the prayer came. His caller called for Zuhr, so the people stood for ablution, performed it, and he led them in prayer; then they sat in circles. When Asr came, the caller called for Asr, and the people rose for ablution again, so he ordered his caller who called out: Beware, no ablution except upon one who has broken it. Knowledge is about to vanish and ignorance to appear, until a man will strike his mother with the sword out of ignorance."
"160","From Ma'mar, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, who said: I do not mind praying five prayers all with a single ablution, so long as I do not suppress stool or urine. From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, the same."
"161","From al-Thawri, from Amr ibn Amir, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: One of us would find ablution sufficient so long as he did not break it."
"162","From al-Thawri, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, from Ibrahim, who said: I pray Zuhr, Asr and Maghrib with a single ablution so long as I do not break it or utter a forbidden word."
"163","From al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, who said: The ablution of none is valid for more than the prayer of a day and night, whether he broke it or not, wiped or not. He said: And I heard Wahb say: ""I pray Zuhr with the ablution of Isha."""
"164","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata': Ablution for every prayer? He said: ""No."" I said: But it says: When you stand for prayer... He said: The first ablution suffices you; had I performed ablution for dawn, I would pray all the prayers with it so long as I did not break it. I said: Is it recommended to perform ablution for every prayer? He said: No."
"165","From Yahya ibn al-Ala', from al-A'mash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, who said: al-Aswad ibn Yazid used to perform ablution with a cup holding about a man's fill, then pray all the prayers with that ablution so long as he did not break it."
"166","From a companion of his, from Abu Dhi'b, from Shu'bah, freedman of Ibn Abbas: that al-Miswar ibn Makhramah said to Ibn Abbas: What about your man Ubayd ibn Umayr, who when he hears the call goes out and performs ablution? Ibn Abbas said: This is what Satan does; when he comes, inform me. When he came, they informed him, and he said: What makes you do what you do? He said: Allah says: When you stand for prayer, wash your faces, and he recited the verse. Ibn Abbas said: ""It is not so; when you have performed ablution, you are pure so long as you do not break it."""
"167","From a man of Egypt, who said: Fudayl ibn Marzuq al-Hamdani reported to us that Ali used to perform ablution for every prayer."
"168","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Nafi' reported to us that Umar used to rinse his mouth and blow his nose for every prayer."
"169","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi': that Ibn Umar used to perform ablution for every prayer."
"170","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Nafi' informed me that Abdullah ibn Umar disliked performing ablution in copper (vessels). He said: Silverware, Rika' and a copper basin were brought to him."
"171","From al-Thawri, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that he would not perform ablution in brass. Sufyan said: ""And we do not follow this."" I said: What is al-nudar? He said: Tamarisk wood."
"172","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, who said: Ibn Umar used to wash his feet in a copper basin. He said: And he disliked drinking in a brass cup."
"173","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata', who said: I mentioned to him Ibn Umar's dislike of copper. He said: There is nothing disliked about ablution in copper except its smell only."
"174","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that he used to perform ablution in copper vessels."
"175","From Ma'mar, from a man, from Nafi': that Ibn Umar disliked performing ablution in copper."
"176","From Ibn Jurayj, from Abdullah ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wash his head in a copper bucket belonging to one of his wives."
"177","From Ma'mar, who said: I asked Abdullah ibn Umar about ablution in copper. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wash his head in a copper bucket belonging to Zaynab bint Jahsh. A man of the family of Jahsh then present said: Yes, that washbasin is with us."
"178","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the illness in which he died: ""Pour over me from seven waterskins whose ties have not been loosened, so I may counsel the people."" A'ishah said: So we seated him in a copper washbasin belonging to Hafsah and poured water over him from them until he began gesturing to us that you have done it; then he went out."
"179","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I was informed from Mu'awiyah that he said: I was forbidden to perform ablution in copper, to approach my wife on the night of the new moon, and when I wake from sleep for prayer, to use the toothstick. He said: It was said to me, I think his saying ""approach my wife on the night of the new moon"" warns people about the new moon and the middle (of the month) because of Satan."
"180","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah say: Umar ibn al-Khattab relieved himself at Ajyad, then returned and asked for water for ablution but they would not give him. Umm Mahzul, one of the nine prostitutes of the Jahiliyyah, said: O Commander of the Believers! Here is water, but it is in an untanned skin container. Umar said to Khalid ibn Tuhayl: Is it so? He said: Yes! He said: ""Bring it, for Allah has made water purifying."""
"181","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: A man asked Ata': Shall I drink and perform ablution from water kept in an untanned container? He said: Is it slaughtered (properly tanned)? He said: Yes, and it is not carrion. He said: There is no harm in that."
"182","From Isra'il, from Isa ibn Abi Azzah, from Amir al-Sha'bi, who said: Tanning of skins is their slaughter."
"183","Abu Sa'id Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad ibn Bishr al-A'rabi reported to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, saying: We read to Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydillah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a sheep belonging to a freedwoman of Maymunah and said: ""Why did you not make use of its hide?"" They said: How, when it is carrion, O Messenger of Allah! He said: ""Only its meat was forbidden."""
"184","From Ma'mar: al-Zuhri used to reject tanning, saying: It may be used in every case."
"185","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata': that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the hide of carrion is tanned, that suffices it, so let him benefit from it."
"186","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard Ata' say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: There was a tame sheep belonging to one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); it died, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Why did you not make use of its hide?"""
"187","Ibn Jurayj reported to us, from Ata', from Ibn Abbas, who said: Maymunah informed me that a sheep died, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Why did you not tan its hide?"""
"188","Ibn Jurayj reported to us, saying: One other than Ata' narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked for water for ablution, and it was said to him: We find for you only in a carrion skin. He said: ""Did you tan it?"" They said: Yes. He said: ""Bring it, for that is purifying."""
"189","From al-Thawri, from Zayd ibn Aslam, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Wa'lah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I said to him: We raid the people of the east and are brought hides and waterskins. He said: I do not know what to say to you, except that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whatever hide is tanned has become pure."""
"190","From Malik ibn Anas, who said: Yazid ibn Abdillah ibn Qusayt narrated to me, from Ibn Thawban, from his mother, from A'ishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that the skins of carrion be used when tanned."
"191","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Tha'labah, from Abu Wa'il, from Umar: that he was asked about carrion and said: Its purification is its tanning."
"192","From al-Thawri, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked for drink and was brought a waterskin. It was said: It is carrion, and tanning was mentioned. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank from it."
"193","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, who said: I asked him about a man who has camels, cattle and sheep that die and their skins are tanned. He said: He may sell them or wear them. From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, the same as Ibrahim's saying."
"194","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata': May a man sell the untanned hides of dead sheep? He said: I would not like him to consume its price, even if tanned."
"195","From Ma'mar, from one who heard al-Hasan say, about the hides of carrion: Its purification is its tanning. He said: And al-Hasan used to say: They may be used, but not sold."
"196","From al-Thawri, from Isa ibn Abi Azzah, from Amir al-Sha'bi, who said: The slaughter of skins is their tanning, so wear it."
"197","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Nafi', freedman of Ibn Umar, reported to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr: that Muhammad ibn al-Ash'ath spoke to A'ishah about making her a quilt of fur. She said: ""It is carrion, and I shall not wear anything of carrion."" He said: Then we shall make for you a quilt and tan it—and she disliked wearing anything of carrion."
"198","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard Ata' asked about young sheep extracted dead from their mothers' bellies and their skins made into furs. He said: ""Are they tanned?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""That suffices; wear them."""
"199","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata' said: We make use of nothing of carrion except its skins; when tanned, its tanning is its purification and its slaughter."
"200","From Abdullah ibn Kathir, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abdullah ibn Ukaym, who said: The letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was read to us in the land of Juhaynah when I was a young lad: Do not make use of anything of carrion, neither hide nor sinew."
"201","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata': What if I am compelled on a journey to water in an untanned carrion container, or to water in which there is a dead mouse, and I have no other water—would you prefer I purify with it or with dust? He said: ""It is dearer to me than dust."" I said: Shall we leave it to settle? He said: ""Yes."" I said: I performed ablution with it settled, unknowing, then prayed the obligatory prayer, then learned before that prayer lapsed. He said: ""Go back, perform ablution, then repeat your prayer."" I said: I learned after it lapsed. He said: Then do not repeat."
"202","From al-Thawri, from Amr, who said: The wool of carrion needs no slaughter; wash it and benefit from it. Al-Thawri said: Do you not see that we pluck it while it is alive?"
"203","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Awn, from Ibn Sirin, who said: Wool, fine wool, shorn wool and fallen wool—there is no harm in it, nor in the feathers of carrion."
"204","From Ma'mar, from Hammad, who said: There is no harm in the wool of carrion, but it is washed; and no harm in the feathers of carrion."
"205","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: A man asked Ata' about the wool of carrion; he disliked it and said: I have not heard a concession except for its hide when tanned."
"206","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata' informed me, saying: They mentioned that lamps are fueled with the fats of carrion, and ships greased with them, without touching; he said: It is taken with a stick. I said: May other than ships be greased with it—leather or something touched? He said: I do not know. I said: And where on ships is it greased? He said: Their backs, not their bellies. I said: Must he not touch its grease with his hand in the lamp? He said: Let him wash his hand when he touches it."
"207","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata': The bones of the elephant? They claim idols are its bones and it is carrion. He said: ""No use may be made of them."" I said: And the bones of dead livestock likewise? He said: ""Yes."" I said: May anything be put in the bones of carrion to mix in? He said: ""No."""
"208","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata': The beast from which ivory combs come is taken dead and made into a handle, for it is not slaughtered. He said: ""No."" Then I reminded him, saying: It is of sea creatures, cast up by the sea. He said: ""Then it is of what the sea casts up."""
"209","From al-Thawri, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, who said: He saw no harm in trading in ivory."
"210","From al-Thawri, from Layth, from Tawus: that he disliked elephant bones. Ma'mar said to me: He saw a pen of elephant bone among my tablets and said: ""Throw it away."" Then Ma'mar later saw with me a pen in the tablets with a silver ring at its end, and said: ""Discard it."""
"211","From Ma'mar ibn Abi Shaybah, who said: I saw beneath Tawus's pillow on his bed a knife whose handle was of hadan (ivory). He said: And he saw it when I lifted the pillow."
"212","From Ma'mar, from Hisham ibn Urwah, who said: My father had a comb and a measure of elephant bone—meaning al-hadan."
"213","From Ma'mar, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Abu Mulayh ibn Usamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade spreading the skins of predators as bedding."
"214","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Abu Shaykh al-Huna'i: that Mu'awiyah said to a group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade spreading the skins of predators."
"215","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Abu Shaykh al-Huna'i: that Mu'awiyah said to a group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Did he forbid leopard saddles to be ridden upon? They said: ""Yes."""
"216","Abbad ibn Kathir al-Basri reported to us, from a man I think Khalid, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Asim ibn Damrah, who said: Ali was brought a beast with a saddle of khazz (silk-wool mix) upon it, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us khazz—riding upon it and sitting upon it—and the skins of leopards—riding upon them and sitting upon them—and spoils to be sold before the fifth is taken, and pregnant enemy captives to be approached, and domestic donkeys, and eating fanged predators and taloned birds, and the price of wine, and the price of carrion, and stud fees, and the price of dogs. From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I was informed from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Asim ibn Damrah, the same."
"217","Ibn Jurayj reported to us, from a man of Banu Zuhrah, raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade riding upon leopard skin."
"218","From Ibn Mujahid, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the skins of predators to be ridden upon. From Ibn Jurayj, from Mujahid, the same."
"219","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from one of his companions, from Umar: that he forbade the skins of predators to be spread or worn."
"220","From al-Thawri, from Suwayd, from Abu Ja'far, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, who said: He had a sanjawiyyah of foxes which he would wear; when he wished to pray, he put it down. Al-sanjawiyyah: a garment dyed sky-color, then placed over fox fur."
"221","From al-Thawri, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, who said: I saw on Ibrahim al-Nakha'i a cap containing fox (fur)."
"222","From al-Thawri, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, who said: A man offered Umar ibn al-Khattab a cap of fox, and he ordered it torn apart."
"223","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab saw on a man a cap containing cat skins, seized it, tore it, and said: I deem it nothing but carrion."
"224","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Sirin, who said: I asked Ubaydah about cat skins; he disliked it, even if tanned."
"225","From al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in the skins of predators being sold, ridden upon and spread."
"226","From Ibn Uyaynah, who said: One who saw al-Sha'bi informed me that he was sitting upon a lion skin."
"227","From Ma'mar, who said: I asked al-Zuhri about leopard skins; he permitted them, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the skins of carrion."
"228","From Humayd, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, who said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: There is no harm in the skins of predators when tanned, saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the skins of carrion. Abd al-Razzaq said: And I heard Ibrahim and others mention from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir."
"229","From Isma'il ibn Abdillah Abu al-Walid, from Ibn Awn, who said: Ibn Sirin used to ride with a saddle covered with leopard skin. He said: And Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz used to ride upon it."
"230","From Isma'il ibn Abdillah, who said: Hisham ibn Urwah informed me that his father had no saddle but with leopard skin upon it."
"231","From Isma'il also, who said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal informed me, from Siraj: he asked al-Hasan about it, and he said: There is no harm in it; it was ridden upon in the time of Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"232","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I asked Ata' about the ablution (water) at the mosque door. He said: There is no harm in it; it was in the time of Ibn Abbas, and he established it, knowing that men and women, black and white, would perform ablution from it, and he saw no harm in it; had there been harm in it, he would have forbidden it. He said: Did you perform ablution from it? He said: ""Yes."""
"233","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata': I saw a man exposed and uncovered at the basin scooping with his hand over his private part. He said: Perform ablution; it is not upon you. The religion is easy. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""Be lenient and leniency will be shown to you."" And those before did not scrutinize this nor press hard in it—meaning: investigate it."
"234","From Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad, who said: Muhammad ibn Wasi' informed me that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, is a new sealed jar dearer to you to perform ablution from, or what people perform ablution from dearer? He said: The dearest religions to Allah is the Hanifiyyah. It was said: What is the Hanifiyyah? He said: ""The lenient."" He said: ""The broad Islam."""
"235","From al-Thawri, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from al-Sha'bi, who said: Your washrooms are dearer to me than a sealed old jar."
"236","From al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, who said: I saw Jarir ibn Abdillah performing ablution from a washroom vessel."
"237","From al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, who said: I heard from Ibrahim, who said: The Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution from al-mihras (a large stone trough)."
"238","From al-Thawri, from Muzahim ibn Zufar, who said: I said to al-Sha'bi: Is a sealed old cup dearer to you to perform ablution from, or these washrooms into which the butcher puts his hand? He said: No, rather these washrooms into which the butcher puts his hand. From Ma'mar, from a man, from Muhammad ibn Wasi', from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same, except he did not mention: the lenient Hanifiyyah."
"239","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: There is no harm in men and women performing ablution together; they are but your halves, sisters, daughters and mothers."
"240","From Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: We used to perform ablution, we and the women, together."
"241","From Isra'il ibn Yunus, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abu Salamah al-Habibi, who said: I saw Umar ibn al-Khattab come to basins with men and women performing ablution together, and he struck them with the stick, then said to the basin owner: Make basins for men and basins for women. Then he met Ali and said: What do you think? He said: I think you are but a shepherd; if you struck them for other than that, you have perished and caused perdition."
"242","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah: that Umar ibn al-Khattab came to water, and it was said to him: Dogs and predators lap from it. He said: It has carried away what it lapped in its bellies. It was said: A dog lapped in the basin of Majannah. He said: ""Did it lap but with its tongue? So he drank from it and drew water."" He said: And Majannah is the name of a basin."
"243","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah: that Umar ibn al-Khattab came to the basin of Majannah, and it was said to him: O Commander of the Believers, a dog just lapped in it. He said: It lapped only with its tongue, so drink from it and perform ablution."
"244","From Malik and others, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib: that he was with Umar ibn al-Khattab in a party including Amr ibn al-As; they stopped at a basin, and Amr said: O owner of the basin, do predators come to your basin? Umar said: O owner of the basin, do not inform us; we come to predators and they come to us. From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, the same."
"245","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdillah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution with the leftover of predators."
"246","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I was informed that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, with Abu Bakr and Umar, to a basin; the people of the water came out and said: O Messenger of Allah, dogs and predators lap in this basin. He said: ""For them what they carried in their bellies, and for us what remains—drink and purification."" The one who informed me doubted that it was the basin of al-Abwa'."
"247","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father: that he sought ablution water for Umar and found it only with a Christian woman; he asked her for it and brought it to Umar, who admired its fineness. Umar said: From where is this? He said to him: From this Christian woman. So he performed ablution, then entered upon her and said to her: ""Accept Islam."" She uncovered her head, and it was like white thaghamah (a white plant). She said: ""After this age?"""
"248","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from a man, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution or drank from a pond into which dog meat was thrown. He said: And I know it only added: and carrion. It was mentioned to him, and he said to him: ""Water—nothing makes it impure."""
"249","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah: that Ibn Abbas said: Water purifies, and is not itself purified."
"250","From Ma'mar, who said: One who heard Ikrimah informed me, saying: Water—nothing makes it impure, and water is purifying."
"251","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I was told that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When water is two qullahs (large jars), it does not carry impurity or harm."
"252","Ibn Jurayj said: They claimed they are the jars of Hajar. Abu Bakr said: Two qullahs are the measure of al-faraq."
"253","From his father, from Ikrimah: that Ibn Abbas passed by a pond with carrion in it; he ordered it removed, then performed ablution from it."
"254","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I was informed from Umar ibn Salm that he heard Ikrimah say: When water is a dhanub or two dhanubs, nothing makes it impure. I said to him: What is al-dhanub? He said: A bucket."
"255","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I was informed from Ibn Mas'ud that he said: When water and blood mix, water is purifying."
"256","From Ma'mar, from a man, from al-Hasan, who said: When a drop of blood falls in water, pour out of it a cup or two; if the water is little, enough to perform ablution from, pour it all out."
"257","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, from Amir ibn Sa'd: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing makes water impure except what changes its smell or taste, or what overcomes its smell and taste."
"258","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: From a man, from Ikrimah, who said: Water—nothing ever makes it impure; it purifies and nothing purifies it. He said: ""And We sent down from the sky purifying water."""
"259","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Abu Bakr ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Bakr ibn Ubaydillah ibn Abdillah ibn Umar, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When water is two qullahs, nothing makes it impure."
"260","From al-Thawri, from Layth: Nothing makes it impure."
"261","From al-Thawri, from a man, from Ibrahim, who said: When water is a kurr, nothing makes it impure; al-kurr is forty dhahab (measures)."
"262","From Ma'mar, who said: I asked al-Zuhri about a hen that fell in a well and died. He said: No harm in performing ablution from it and drinking, unless it stinks so its stench is found in the water, then it is drawn out."
"263","From Ma'mar, who said: I asked al-Zuhri about a mouse that fell in the well. He said: If taken out at once, no harm; if it died in it, it (the well) is drawn out."
"264","From Ma'mar, who said: One who heard al-Hasan informed me, saying: When an animal dies in the well, water is taken from it; if it disintegrates in it, it is drawn out."
"265","From Ma'mar, who said: One who heard al-Hasan informed me, saying: When an animal dies in the well, forty buckets are taken from it."
"266","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father: that Ali said: When a mouse falls in the well and breaks apart, seven buckets are drawn from it; if the mouse is intact, unbroken, one or two buckets are drawn from it; if it is stinking, worse than that, then draw from the well what removes the smell."
"267","From Layth, from Ata', who said: When a dog falls in the well and is taken out at once, twenty buckets are drawn from it; if taken out when dead, sixty or seventy buckets are drawn from it; if it disintegrates in it, its water is drawn out; if they cannot, one hundred and twenty buckets are drawn from it."
"268","From Ma'mar, who said: A man fell in Zamzam and died in it, so Ibn Abbas ordered its springs blocked and it drawn out. It was said to him: There is a spring that has overcome us. ""It is from Paradise."" So he gave them a khazz cloak and they stuffed it in it, then its water was drawn out until no stench remained in it."
"269","From al-Thawri, from Mujahid and Ata', about a mouse that fell in a well and bread was kneaded with its water. He said: ""It is fed to chickens."""
"270","From a man of Basra: that Amr ibn Ubayd said to al-Hasan: I put my ablution water and a mouse comes and drinks from it. Al-Hasan said: Pour it out, for the wicked one drinks nothing but urinates in it. Tawbah mentioned it from Shadid ibn Abi al-Hakam."
"271","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a mouse falling in ghee. He said: If solid, throw it and what is around it; if liquid, do not approach it. And from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydillah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah; and likewise Ibn Uyaynah reported to us from Ma'mar, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, similar. Abu Harun said: We said to Abu Sa'id: May it be used? He said: ""Yes."""
"272","From Ma'mar, from Abu Harun, from Abu Sa'id, who said: Benefit from it, but do not eat it."
"273","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Sharik ibn Abi Namir, from Ata' ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a mouse falling in ghee. He said: If solid, what is around it to the measure of a palm is taken, and the rest eaten."
"274","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Abu Jabir al-Bayadi, from Ibn al-Musayyib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a mouse falling in ghee. He said: If solid, what is around it to the measure of a palm is taken; and if it falls in oil, it is used for lamps."
"275","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata': A mouse falls in solid or non-solid fat? He said: It reached us: if solid, what is around it is taken and thrown, and the rest eaten. I said: And non-solid? He said: Nothing reached me about it, but I think it be used for lamps and not eaten."
"276","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, who said: When a mouse dies in solid fat. He said: It reached us: if solid, what is around it is taken and thrown, and the rest eaten."
"277","From Ma'mar and al-Thawri, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: about a mouse that fell in oil, twenty qartala (measures). Ibn Umar said: Use it for lamps and grease hides with it."
"278","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Amr ibn Dinar: A mouse died in a man's oil with which he oils himself. He said: I do not like it."
"279","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I asked Ata' about a mouse that died in honey. He said: Honey is like solid; what is around it is scooped, and the rest eaten."
"280","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata': I said to him: A mouse dies in melted ghee or oil and is found skinned, or found dead intact, unskinned. He said: It is the same; the oil is heated and used for oiling if not foul. I said: And the ghee is heated then eaten? He said: ""What is eaten is not like something on the head used for oiling."""
"281","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata': A mouse fell in a jar and died in it. He said: No ablution from it; if you performed ablution unknowing, then prayed unknowing, repeat while in the time. He said: If the time lapsed, repeat also. I said: My garment touched some of that jar's water—shall I wash or sprinkle it? He said: ""No."""
"282","From al-Thawri, who said: When compelled to water in which a mouse fell, perform ablution and tayammum—combine both."
"283","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata': A gecko dies in fat—ghee, oil and the like—is it like the mouse in that? He said: ""And I hold (it so)."""
"284","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin: that a gecko fell in ghee of the family of Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, and they mixed porridge with it, then informed him. He said: Sell it to one who deems it lawful, then inform him."
"285","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I was informed from Imran ibn Husayn: that a gecko died belonging to them, and they mixed porridge with it and he drank of it, then was informed of the matter. He said: Did you know? They said: No. He clapped his hands and said: Sell the ghee and porridge to those of other than your religion, and clarify to them the matter. One of his family said: Shall we not use it for lamps? He said: Yes, if you wish."
"286","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata': A dung beetle dies in honey, ghee, fat or water. He said: It is but a husk, without flesh or blood; if it falls in solid or non-solid and dies, nothing is thrown of it, do not pour it out, eat it. I said to him: What is al-ju'al? He said: The black creature that rolls dung."
"287","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, about dung beetles, hornets and the like falling in water, or in food and drink. He said: It is eaten, drunk, and ablution performed from it; whatever is in water without bone, there is no harm in it."
"288","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Manbudh, from his mother: that she used to travel with Maymunah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: We would come to a pond with dead dung beetles in it and take water from it—meaning: they would drink it."
"289","From al-Thawri, from his father, from Ibrahim: that he was asked about a fly falling in water and dying in it. He said: There is no harm in it."
"290","From Ma'mar, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you urinate in stagnant water that does not flow, then perform ablution from it."
"291","Maamar reported from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should urinate into standing water and then perform ablution from it."
"292","From Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman ibn Musa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to urinate into stagnant collected water."
"293","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Dhakwan, from Musa ibn Abi Uthman, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade urinating into standing water that does not flow and then bathing in it."
"294","Ibn Jurayj reported from Sulayman ibn Musa, from a man, who said: I asked Jabir ibn Abd Allah about stagnant water - may I bathe in it when a person in janabah has entered it? He said: No, but scoop out of it by handfuls."
"295","From Maamar, from a man of the people of Kufa, that Ibn Abbas said: If janabah befalls you and you pass by a pond, then scoop from it with a scooping and pour it over yourself, and if some of it drips back into it, do not mind, but do not enter into it if you are able."
"296","From Maamar, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, concerning a man in janabah who passes by a well and has no bucket with him: he said, If he finds no way except to put his hand into it, let him put it in. Maamar said: And I heard someone saying: He wets the edge of his garment, then wrings it over his hands, and washes his hands. Maamar said: Had he performed tayammum and then put in his hand, it would be dearer to me."
"297","From Maamar, from Qatadah, concerning a man who forgot and put his hand into the water he bathes with while in janabah before washing his hands: he said, Evil is what he did, but he may bathe with it."
"298","From Maamar, he said: One who heard al-Hasan informed me, saying: He throws it away, and does not perform ablution nor ghusl with it."
"299","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I asked Ata about a person in janabah who forgets and puts his hand into the vessel containing his ghusl water before washing his hands. He said: If he forgot, there is no harm; let him wash his hands."
"300","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no janabah upon a garment, nor janabah upon the ground, nor janabah upon a man touched by a person in janabah, nor janabah upon water - meaning: if his hands precede him and he puts them into water while in janabah before washing them, there is no harm."
"301","From Maamar, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, he said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to put their hands into water while in janabah, and women while menstruating, and that did not spoil anything for them."
"302","From Maamar, he said: I asked al-Zuhri about a man bathing from janabah when some water from his skin splashes into the vessel. He said: There is no harm in it."
"303","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: What about what splashes from the vessel into the basin? He said: It will not harm you."
"304","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: May I place my cup containing my ablution water into the basin in which I perform ablution, though it may be large? He said: No. I said: But I know that splashing from the basin falls upon me while the cup is not in it, and splashing from the basin falls into my ablution water while the cup is not in it. He said: None of that harms you; it is excused for you that this happens, though you had set it aside and some from the basin entered it."
"305","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Nafi: Where did Ibn Umar place his vessel from which he performed ablution? He said: Beside him."
"306","From al-Thawri, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from a man, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Abbas: he was asked about a man who bathes or performs ablution using water while some of it splashes back into it. He said: He saw no harm in it."
"307","From Maamar, from one who heard Anas ibn Malik and al-Hasan, both being asked about a man bathing from janabah when some of his washing water splashes into the water he is bathing from. He said: There is no harm in it."
"308","From Maamar, from Jafar ibn Burqan, he said: Maymun ibn Mihran used to bathe from a vessel and lift it up, so that none of his washing water would splash into it."
"309","From Maamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from a man of the Ansar, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: Two waters do not purify from janabah: seawater and bathhouse water."
"310","Maamar said: I asked Yahya about it after a while, and he said: Something more reliable than that has reached me: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about seawater, and he said: The water of the sea is purifying, and its dead animals are lawful."
"311","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa informed me, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sea is purifying, its water is purifying and its dead animals are lawful. From al-Thawri, from Aban, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"312","From al-Thawri and Ibn Uyaynah, from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Mughirah ibn Abd Allah, that some people of Banu Mudlij asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): We ride upon rafts of ours, and each of us carries only a little water for his drinking; if we perform ablution with seawater we feel uneasy within ourselves, and if we perform ablution from our drinking water we will go thirsty. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is purifying, its water is purifying and its dead animals are lawful."
"313","From Maamar, from Ayyub, from Abu Yazid al-Madani, he said: A man of the fishermen who fish at al-Jar narrated to me - and the people of Madinah used to be supplied from al-Jar - that he found scattered grain, and Umar began picking it up until he gathered about a mudd of it, or close to a mudd, then said: Do I not see you doing the like of this, though this is the sustenance of a Muslim man until night? He said: So I said to him: O Commander of the Believers, if only you would ride along to see how we fish? He said: So he rode with them and they began fishing, and Umar said: By Allah, I have never seen an earning as wholesome as today - or he said: as lawful. Then he said: So we prepared food for him, and I said: O Commander of the Believers, if you wish we will give you broth to drink, and if you wish water, for milk is easier for us than water here; we bring sweet water from such-and-such a place. He said: So he ate, then called for whichever he wanted, then we said: O Commander of the Believers, we go out to this place and carry water with us for our drinking, then we perform ablution with seawater. He said: Glory be to Allah! And what water is purer than the water of the sea?"
"314","From Ibn al-Taymi, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, that Umar ibn al-Khattab was asked about seawater, and he said: What water is purer than the water of the sea?"
"315","From Maamar, from Qatadah: Ibn Abbas said: They are two seas: this one sweet and fresh, and this one salty and bitter."
"316","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa asked Ata, while I was listening: Is the water of the sea purifying? He said: Yes."
"317","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: What if I find water other than seawater, and al-ida, and I see a well - do I leave the well and al-ida? He said: If you purify yourself from either of them, both are purifying. I said to him: What is al-ida? He said: The vessel for purification water."
"318","From al-Thawri, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, he said: I asked Ibrahim about seawater - may I bathe with it? He said: Yes, though sweet water is dearer to me."
"319","From Maamar and Ibn Jurayj, both said: Ibn Tawus informed us, from his father, that a man said to him: I passed by the sea while in janabah and bathed from it. He said: That suffices you."
"320","From Maamar, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The purification of the vessel of one of you, when a dog laps in it, is to wash it seven times."
"321","From Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a dog laps in a vessel, wash it seven times, the first of them with dust. From Maamar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"322","From Maamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said, concerning a dog that laps in a vessel: Do not put anything in it until you wash it seven times."
"323","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: How many times is a vessel lapped in by a dog washed? He said: All of that I have heard: seven, five, and three times."
"324","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar said: A vessel lapped in by a dog is washed seven times."
"325","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ziyad informed me that Thabit ibn Iyad, the freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd, narrated to him that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times. Ziyad said: And Hilal ibn Usamah informed me that he heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"326","From Maamar, he said: I asked al-Zuhri about a dog that laps in a vessel. He said: It is washed three times. He said: I have not heard anything about the cat."
"327","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A dog lapped in the large bowl of some people containing milk, and they caught it at that moment and scooped away around what it had lapped in. He said: Do not drink it."
"328","From Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he used to dislike the leftover of a dog. From al-Thawri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, the like of it."
"329","From Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he used to dislike the leftover of the cat. From al-Thawri, from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, the like of it."
"330","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: What about the cat? He said: It is in the position of the dog, or worse than it."
"331","From Maamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, concerning the cat that laps in a vessel: he said, It is in the position of the dog; it is washed seven times."
"332","Maamar reported from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, concerning the cat that laps in a vessel: he said, Wash it once and pour it away."
"333","From Maamar, from Qatadah, he said: I asked Ibn al-Musayyab about the cat that laps in a vessel. He said: It is washed once or twice. And al-Hasan used to say: Once or three times."
"334","From Maamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, that he saw Abu Qatadah al-Ansari placing a vessel for the cat so it drank from it, then performing ablution with its leftover. From al-Thawri, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, the like of it."
"335","From Maamar and Ibn Jurayj, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, that he heard Ikrimah, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, saying: Abu Qatadah brought a vessel close to the cat and it lapped in it, then he performed ablution from its leftover, and said: It is among the furnishings of the house. Maamar, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, the like of it."
"336","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, he said: Salih, the freedman of al-Tawamah, informed me, he said: I heard Abu Qatadah saying: There is no harm in ablution with the leftover of the cat, for it is only among my dependents. From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from a woman, from her mother - who was married to Abu Qatadah - the like of the hadith of Malik."
"337","From Ibn Jurayj, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah, from a woman, from her mother - who was married to Abu Qatadah - that her mother informed her that Abu Qatadah visited them, so they poured ablution water for him; a cat came near it, so he inclined toward it the vessel containing his ablution water and it drank from it, then he performed ablution with its leftover, and they marvelled at that. Abu Qatadah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is not impure; it is among those that go around among you."
"338","From Malik ibn Anas, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from Humaydah bint Ubayd ibn Rifaa, from Kabshah bint Kab ibn Malik - who was married to the son of Abu Qatadah - that Abu Qatadah entered upon her and she poured ablution water for him; a cat came and drank, so he inclined the vessel for it until it drank. Kabshah said: He saw me looking at him, so he said: Do you marvel, O daughter of my brother? She said: Yes. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not impure; it is only among the male and female household goers-around."
"339","From Maamar, from Abu Ishaq, he said: A cat lapped in some milk belonging to the family of Abu Qays, and its people wanted to pour the milk away, so he forbade them that and ordered them to drink it."
"340","From Ibn Jurayj, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from a freedman of the Ansar, that his grandmother informed him that her mistress sent her with some porridge - or rice - to Aishah as a gift; she brought it while Aishah was praying, so she placed it down, and a cat came near it and ate from it, while there were women with Aishah. When she finished, she called for it, and when she saw the women avoiding the place from which the cat had eaten, Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, placed her hand upon the place in which the cat had eaten and said: It is not impure."
"341","From al-Thawri, from Harithah ibn Abi al-Rijal, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: I used to perform ablution, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from a vessel from which a cat had taken before that."
"342","From al-Thawri, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi ibn Umaylah al-Fazari, from a paternal aunt of his called Safiyyah bint Umaylah, from Husayn ibn Ali, that a woman asked about the cat that laps in my drink. He said: The cat? She said: Yes. He said: Do not pour away your drink nor your purification water, for it does not make anything impure."
"343","From Maamar, from Qatadah and Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The cat is among the furnishings of the house."
"344","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, he said: Ibn Abbas was asked about a cat lapping in a vessel - is it washed? He said: It is only among the furnishings of the house."
"345","From al-Thawri, from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah, from Ibrahim, he said: The cat is among the furnishings of the house."
"346","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Sadaqah ibn Yasar informed me, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once performed ablution and was held back from his Companions, then he came out, and they said: What held you back? He said: A little creature from which the cat drank. Sadaqah said: I do not know whether it was from his ablution water or from the leftover of his ablution water, I do not know. And a man then present among those who had heard knowledge said: Rather, from his ablution water."
"347","From Ibn Jurayj: I said to Ata: A donkey drinks in my large bowl? He said: Yes, and perform ablution with its leftover. Then he recited: And horses and mules and donkeys for you to ride. I said: But its eating is forbidden? He said: Its being eaten is not like performing ablution with its leftover; so give it to drink in your bowl."
"348","From Ibn Mujahid, from his father, that he used to perform ablution with the leftover of a donkey."
"349","From Maamar, from a man who saw Mujahid performing ablution with the leftover of a donkey."
"350","From Maamar, he said: I asked al-Zuhri about ablution with the leftover of a donkey. He said: There is no harm in it."
"351","And Maamar said, and one who heard al-Hasan informed me, saying: There is no harm in performing ablution with the leftover of a donkey."
"352","From his father, from Abd al-Karim, he said: I asked al-Hasan about the leftover of a donkey, and he said: There is no harm in the leftover of all riding animals."
"353","He said: And I asked Ibrahim al-Nakhai about the leftover of a donkey? And he disliked it."
"354","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, from al-Hasan, he said: There is no harm in the leftover of a donkey."
"355","From Hisham, from al-Hasan, he said: There is no harm in performing ablution with the leftover of a donkey."
"356","From al-Thawri, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim: He disliked the leftover of the donkey, the mule, and the dog, and saw no harm in the leftover of the horse, nor the sheep. From Hushaym, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, the like of it."
"357","From Maamar, from Qatadah, that he disliked performing ablution with the leftover of a donkey. He said: And is it anything but the donkey?"
"358","From Maamar, from Qatadah, he said: Whatever animal whose flesh you do not eat, do not perform ablution with its leftover. Qatadah said: And I have not heard anyone differ concerning animals whose flesh is eaten, that one may perform ablution with its leftover and drink from it."
"359","From Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he used to dislike the leftover of the donkey, the dog, and the cat - that one perform ablution with their leftover. From al-Thawri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, the like of it."
"360","From Maamar, from Qatadah, he said: I asked al-Hasan and Ibn al-Musayyab about ablution with the leftover of a woman, and both of them forbade me it."
"361","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Ubayd informed me, from al-Hasan, that he saw no harm in a man and a woman sharing ablution water, and saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to perform ablution with the leftover of a woman."
"362","From Maamar, from Jabir ibn Yazid al-Jufi, from a relative of Juwayriyah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she said: Do not perform ablution with the leftover of my ablution."
"363","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Umar ibn Said ibn Masruq, from a man, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari, from a man who accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for three years, that he said: He forbade a man to perform ablution with the leftover of a woman."
"364","From Maamar, he said: I heard Qatadah - or another - narrating from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that he saw no harm in the leftover drink of a woman, nor in the leftover of her ablution, and saying: She is cleaner in garments and sweeter in scent. From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Ayyub, from a man, from Ibn Abbas, the like of it."
"365","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: A man asked Ata, saying: A woman bathes though not in janabah - may a man bathe with her leftover? He said: Yes."
"366","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Abbas ibn Abd Allah ibn Mabad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no harm in the leftover of a woman, whether menstruating or not, when there is nothing wrong with her hands."
"367","From Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: There is no harm in a man performing ablution with the leftover of a woman, so long as she is not menstruating or in janabah."
"368","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: I meet a woman at the water bathing with it or performing ablution - may a man perform ablution with her leftover? He said: Yes, if she is a Muslim. Ata said: A man may bathe with the leftover of a woman, other than two persons in janabah together."
"369","From Maamar, from Asim ibn Sulayman: I heard Abd Allah ibn Sarjis saying: There is no harm in a man and a woman bathing from a single vessel, but if she is alone with it, do not approach it."
"370","From Maamar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: There is no harm in ablution with the leftover drink of a woman and the leftover of her ablution, so long as she is not in janabah or menstruating; but if she is alone with it, do not approach it."
"371","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: A man asked Ata, saying: A woman bathes though not in janabah - may a man bathe with a vessel along with her? He said: Yes."
"372","From al-Thawri, from Miqdam ibn Shurayh ibn Hani, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I used to drink from a vessel while menstruating, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take it and place his mouth upon the place of my mouth and drink, and I would take the bone with meat and bite from it, then he would take it from me and place his mouth upon the place of my mouth and bite from it."
"373","From Maamar, he said: I asked al-Zuhri about the leftover of a menstruating woman and a person in janabah, and he saw no harm in it."
"374","From Maamar, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, he said: There is no harm in the leftover of a menstruating woman and a person in janabah, and he saw no harm in it as ablution water or drink - meaning: and he saw no harm in it."
"375","From Maamar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, he said: There is no harm in the leftover of a menstruating woman - that one drink it and perform ablution from it."
"376","From al-Thawri, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim: He used to dislike the leftover of a person in janabah, his ablution water and his drink, and saw no harm in performing ablution with the leftover of a menstruating woman, though he disliked the leftover of her drink. From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, from al-Hasan, the like of the hadith of Maamar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan."
"377","From Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he used to dislike the leftover of a menstruating woman and a person in janabah."
"378","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Abbas ibn Abd Allah ibn Mabad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no harm in the leftover of a woman, whether menstruating or not."
"379","From al-Thawri, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bathed from janabah, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and performed ablution with her leftover. She said: I have bathed from it. He said: Water is not made impure by anything. From Israil, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, the like of it."
"380","From Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab was asked about a menstruating woman handing a man his ablution water, putting her hand into it. He said: Her menstruation is not in her hand."
"381","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: May a person in janabah perform ablution with the leftover ablution water of another in janabah, and may a man and a woman each perform ablution with the leftover of the other when both are in janabah? He said: As for prayer, then no; but for food and drink and sleep. He said: No benefit is taken from the leftover ablution water of one in janabah for prayer. I said: And is the menstruating woman in their position? He said: Yes."
"382","From Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: We used to bathe in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we and our wives, from a single vessel."
"383","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata said: There is no harm in a pure woman combing her hair with the leftover janabah water of one in janabah, and in dyeing with her leftover; either of them may eat and drink from the leftover of the other."
"384","From Maamar, from al-Zuhri, and from Jabir, from al-Shabi, he said: There is no harm in a pure woman combing her hair with the leftover of a menstruating woman. From Maamar, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, the like of it."
"385","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I asked Ata about touching the armpit. He said: I do not like to touch it since I heard what I heard about it from Umar ibn al-Khattab, yet I do not perform ablution from it."
"386","From Ibrahim, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from a man, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, he said: Whoever touches his armpit, let him perform ablution. He said: And I have heard this hadith only from him. He said: And we narrate to people ablution from touching the private part, yet they do not believe us - so how if we narrated touching the armpit? From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, the like of it, except that he did not mention the private part."
"387","From Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, he said: Ibn Umar used to pass his hand over his armpit when performing ablution, then not repeat ablution."
"388","From Abu Jafar al-Razi, he said: Yahya al-Bakka informed us, he said: I saw Ibn Umar in a waist-wrapper and cloak, and I saw him placing his hand upon his nose, then striking his armpit with his hand while in prayer."
"389","From Maamar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, and from a man, from al-Hasan, he said: There is no ablution in plucking the armpit."
"390","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Shuayb, that Busrah bint Safwan ibn Muharrath said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, one of us performs ablution for prayer and finishes her ablution, then puts her hand inside her shift and touches her private part - is ablution obligatory upon her? He said: Yes; when she touches her private part, let her repeat the prayer and the ablution. He said: And Abd Allah ibn Amr was sitting, yet that did not alarm Abd Allah ibn Amr thereafter."
"391","From Maamar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: He and Marwan discussed ablution from touching the private part; Marwan said: Busrah bint Safwan narrated to me that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanding ablution from touching the private part. As though Urwah was not convinced by his hadith, so Marwan sent a policeman to her, and he returned and informed them that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanding ablution from touching the private part. Maamar said: And Hisham ibn Urwah informed me, from his father, the like of it."
"392","Ibn Jurayj reported, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from Urwah, that he used to narrate from Busrah bint Safwan, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you touches his penis, let him perform ablution."
"393","From Maamar ibn Rashid, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the dawn prayer then returned to it. It was said to him: You had already prayed. He said: Yes, but I touched my penis and forgot to perform ablution."
"394","From Ibn Jurayj, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, that Mujahid informed him that a member of the sons of Sad ibn Abi Waqqas informed him, he said: I used to hold the mushaf for Sad ibn Abi Waqqas while he was revising it, until my penis itched me and I scratched it; when he saw me putting my hand there, he said: Did you touch it? I said: Yes. He said: Stand and perform ablution."
"395","From Maamar and Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Hurrah, from Musab ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: I used to recite before my father, holding the mushaf while he read it, then my penis itched me and I put in my hand and scratched it; then I found I had touched my penis, and I mentioned that to him. He said: Stand and perform ablution, so I did."
"396","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah narrating, from one I do not suspect, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, while standing leading the people in prayer when he had begun the prayer, let his hand slip onto his penis; so he gestured to the people to stay, went and performed ablution, then came and prayed. His father said to him: Perhaps he found madhiy? He said: I do not know."
"397","From Maamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, that Ibn Umar led them in the Asr prayer, then travelled some miles - he thought he said: six - then dismounted, performed ablution, and repeated the prayer. He said: So I said to him: Had you not already prayed? He said: Yes, but I had touched my penis and prayed without performing ablution, so for that I repeated."
"398","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Shihab informed us, from Salim, that Ibn Umar led them in Asr prayer on the road to Makkah, then we rode and travelled as much as was decreed, then Ibn Umar halted, performed ablution, and prayed Asr alone. Salim said: So I said to him: You already led us in Asr prayer - have you forgotten? He said: I have not forgotten, but I had touched my penis before praying; when I remembered that, I performed ablution and repeated my prayer. Ibn Jurayj said: And Hasan ibn Muslim narrated to me that Salim narrated to him close to this hadith of Ibn Shihab, except that he did not mention which prayer."
"399","From Maamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, he said: My father used to bathe, then perform ablution, saying: Does not ghusl suffice you? And he would say: Yes, but it seems to me that something comes out of my penis and I touch it, so I perform ablution for that."
"400","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: What if you touch your penis while bathing? He said: Then I would return with an ablution."
"401","From Abd Allah ibn Muharrar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Whoever touches his penis, let him perform ablution."
"402","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: Whoever touches his penis, let him perform ablution."
"403","And that was only transmitted from Ibn Umar: Qays said to him: O Abu Muhammad, had you touched your penis while in an obligatory prayer, would you leave and break your prayer to perform ablution? He said: Yes; by Allah, I would break my prayer and perform ablution."
"404","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: I touched the penis from behind the garment. He said: There is no ablution except from direct contact, then by touching. I said: With the thigh or the shin? He said: There is no ablution except with the hand. I said: So what distinguishes between that? He said: It is only from the leg - and how would the leg not touch? The hand is not like the leg in that."
"405","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: What if I touch my penis without touching the urinary passage? He said: If you touch its back, or whichever part it be, then perform ablution."
"406","From Israil ibn Yunus, from Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: I touched my penis while praying. He said: No harm; it is only a piece of flesh of yours."
"407","From Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Jabir, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about a man who performs ablution and his hand falls and touches his penis - does he perform ablution? Then I let my hands fall and touched my penis? He said: It is part of you."
"408","From Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, he said: A group of the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered, among them one saying: I do not mind whether I touch it, or my ear, or my thigh, or my knee."
"409","From Maamar and al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, he said: I do not mind whether I touch it or my ear, when I do not intend that deliberately."
"410","From Maamar, from Qatadah, from al-Makhariq ibn Ahmar al-Kulai, he said: I heard Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman; and from Iyad ibn Laqit, he said: Al-Bara ibn Qays narrated to us, he said: I heard Hudhayfah, when a man asked him about touching the penis in prayer, saying: I do not mind whether I touch it or touch my nose. And Sufyan holds to this."
"411","From Maamar, from al-Thawri and Israil, from Ishaq, from Arqam ibn Shurahbil, he said: I scratched my body while in prayer and reached my penis, so I said to Abd Allah ibn Masud - and he laughed and said: Cut it off, where will you put it away? It is only a piece of flesh of yours."
"412","From Maamar, from Qatadah, from Said ibn Jubayr, that Ibn Masud said: I do not mind whether I touch it or the tip of my nose."
"413","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: What if I touch the penis with the forearm - do I perform ablution? He said: Yes."
"414","Maamar reported from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, he said: I do not mind whether I touch it or my thigh."
"415","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: A man asked Sad ibn Abi Waqqas about touching the penis - does one perform ablution from it? He said: If there is anything impure of yours, then cut it off."
"416","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed me, from Kathir among the people of Madinah, that Ibn Abbas said to Ibn Umar: Had I known that what you say about the penis is true, I would cut it off; indeed, had I known it impure, I would cut it off. And I do not mind whether I touch it or touch my nose."
"417","From Sulayman ibn Mihran al-Amash, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Qays ibn al-Sakan, that Ali, Abd Allah ibn Masud, Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, and Abu Hurayrah do not see ablution from touching the penis, and they said: There is no harm in it."
"418","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Whoever touches his penis, there is no ablution upon him."
"419","From Maamar, he said: Al-Hasan and Qatadah used not to see ablution in it."
"420","From al-Thawri, he said: I heard him saying: One of their commanders summoned me and Ibn Jurayj and asked us about touching the penis; Ibn Jurayj said: He performs ablution. And I said: No ablution upon him. When we differed, I said to Ibn Jurayj: What if a man placed his hand upon semen? He said: He washes his hand. I said: So which of the two is more impure, semen or the penis? He said: No, rather semen. He said: So I said: Then how is this? He said: None but a devil cast it upon your tongue."
"421","Reported from Maamar, he said: Al-Hasan and Qatadah used not to see ablution in it."
"422","Maamar reported from al-Zuhri, he said: I heard Aban ibn Uthman saying: Whoever touches the penis, let him perform ablution."
"423","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, that he said: Whoever touches his inner thighs, let him perform ablution. Amr said: And I think it means only the creases of the thighs."
"424","That he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever touches his penis, or his testicles, or his thigh-creases, let him repeat ablution."
"425","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: What if I touch what is around the penis and the testicles? He said: There is no ablution except from it itself."
"426","From Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: When a man touches his testicles or his thigh-creases, he performs ablution."
"427","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man touches his sitting-place, the excretory passage, without placing his hand there - does he perform ablution? He said: Yes; if you would perform ablution from touching the penis while in ablution, you would perform ablution from touching it. He said: I said: What if he touches what is around the excretory passage without inserting his hand there?"
"428","From Maamar, he said: I heard a man saying to Qatadah: A man afflicted with piles whose sitting-place protrudes from severe straining and he puts it back with his hand - is ablution upon him? He said: No, but let him wash his hand."
"429","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: What if I touch the penis of a small boy? He said: Perform ablution."
"430","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: I touched the sheath of a donkey, or the teats of a camel. He said: As for the sheath of the donkey, you would be in ablution - meaning you must perform ablution anew - and as for the teats of the camel, then no. I said: So what distinguishes between them? I said: Because of the donkey, for it is more impure. He said: And I say: I consider everything impure in the form of the donkey whose flesh is not eaten - whoever touches that part of it, ablution is upon him; and everything whose flesh is eaten, in the form of the camel - whoever touches that part of it, there is no ablution from it."
"431","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A dog touched my garment - shall I sprinkle it? He said: No."
"432","From Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: I asked him, saying: A dog passed and touched my cloak. He said: If anything stuck to it, wash it; otherwise there is no harm."
"433","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: If a man touches a dog or a donkey while moist, does he perform ablution from it? He said: No, and that is fouler than the armpit."
"434","From Maamar, from Hammad, concerning a man who performed ablution then touched a dog: he said, There is no ablution upon him."
"435","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: A man asked Ata, saying: I touched my sandals in prayer, and my hands fell upon filth in them - do I repeat my prayer? He said: No."
"436","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: I asked him about a man who performs ablution then shakes hands with a person in major impurity, a menstruating woman, a Jew and a Christian; he said: He does not repeat the ablution."
"437","From Ma'mar, from Qatada: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Hudhayfa and extended his hand toward Hudhayfa; Hudhayfa said: I am in major impurity; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer does not become impure."
"438","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no janaba upon a man touched by a man in janaba; from Ma'mar, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, the same."
"439","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, from Ibn Sirin, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, he said: Ibn Mas'ud prayed while on his belly there was dung and blood from slaughtered camels he had slaughtered, and he did not perform ablution."
"440","From al-Thawri, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Ibn Sirin, he said: Ibn Mas'ud slaughtered a camel and got stained with its blood and dung, then the prayer was established and he prayed and did not perform ablution."
"441","From Ibn Uyayna, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani or another, that Ali called al-Mustawrid al-Ijli to repent while he intended prayer, and said: I seek Allah's help against you; he said: And I seek the help of Christ against you; he said: So Ali reached with his hand to his neck, found a cross and cut it off; when he entered the prayer he put a man forward and left, then he informed the people that he did not do that because of a ritual impurity he had caused, but because he had touched these impurities and wished to renew ablution from them."
"442","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: Trimming the mustache and clipping the nails, is ablution due from it? He said: No, but let him touch with water where he clipped and trimmed."
"443","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: When a man takes something from his nails or his hair, he passes water over it."
"444","From Ma'mar, from a man, from al-Hakam ibn Utayba, he said: He wipes water over it."
"445","From Ma'mar, from Hammad, he said: His ablution has been broken."
"446","From Hisham, from al-Hasan regarding one who takes from his nails and hair: There is nothing upon him."
"447","From al-Thawri, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: There is nothing upon him."
"448","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, he said: It is purification."
"449","From Ma'mar and al-Thawri, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: That I perform ablution due to a foul word is dearer to me than that I perform ablution due to good food."
"450","From al-Thawri, from Asim, from Dhakwan, that Aisha said: One of you performs ablution due to good food, yet does not perform ablution due to the shameful word he utters."
"451","From al-Thawri, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, from Ibrahim, he said: I pray Zuhr, Asr and Maghrib with one ablution, unless I cause impurity or utter evil; from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ibn Sirin, from Ubayda, the same."
"452","From Ma'mar, he said: I asked al-Zuhri: Do you know of ablution due to any speech? He said: No."
"453","From Ma'mar, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: Ablution is due to ritual impurity."
"454","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata said: When sleep overcomes, then perform ablution, sitting or lying down."
"455","From Hisham, from al-Hasan, he said: When he sleeps sitting or standing, then ablution is due."
"456","From Ma'mar, from a man, from al-Hasan, he said: When a man becomes heavy with sleep, standing, sitting or lying down, he performs ablution; he said: And al-Hasan used to perform ablution several times in a night."
"457","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, he said: I asked al-Hasan about a man who sleeps while prostrating; he said: When sleep mixes with him, let him perform ablution; he said: And we saw al-Hasan in the maqsura nodding his head, then standing and praying without performing ablution."
"458","From al-Thawri, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Ablution is obligatory upon every sleeper, except one who nods lightly with his head."
"459","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: When he sleeps while sitting a heavy sleep, he repeats the ablution; as for a light doze, there is no harm."
"460","From Ja'far ibn Sulayman and others, from Sa'id al-Jurayri, from Hilal al-Absi, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, he said: Whoever is overcome by sleep, upon him is ablution."
"461","From Malik ibn Anas, from Zayd ibn Aslam, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Whoever sleeps lying down, let him perform ablution."
"462","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, from Anas, he said: I saw the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being awakened for prayer, and I would hear snoring from some of them, meaning while sitting, and they would not perform ablution; Ma'mar said: So I narrated it to al-Zuhri, and a man with him said: Or khateetan; al-Zuhri said: No, he got ghatitan correct."
"463","From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar that he would sleep while sitting and not perform ablution, and when he slept lying down he would repeat the ablution; from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, the same."
"464","From al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Thabit ibn Ubayd, he said: I came to Ibn Umar while he was sitting waiting for the prayer, so I greeted him and he woke up, and said: O Abu Thabit! He said: I said: Yes; he said: Did you greet? He said: I said: Yes; he said: When you greet, make them hear, and when they reply to you, let them make you hear; then he stood and prayed, though he had been sitting with knees drawn up and had slept."
"465","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibrahim ibn Maysara, that Tawus came on Friday while Ibn al-Dahhak was addressing the people; he said: When we prayed and left, he said: What did he say when I dozed?"
"466","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: I asked him about a man who sleeps while bowing or prostrating; he said: Ablution is not obligatory upon him until he lays his side down."
"467","From Ibn al-Taymi, from Fitr, from Ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Abi Umayya, that Ali, Ibn Mas'ud and al-Sha'bi said regarding a man who sleeps while sitting: There is no ablution upon him."
"468","From Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: I asked Ubayda about a man who sleeps while prostrating, does he perform ablution? He said: He knows himself best."
"469","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, he said: I asked Ubayda: Does a man perform ablution when he sleeps? He said: He knows himself best."
"470","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: I dozed briefly during the obligatory prayer, then started and did not know whether I uttered anything; do I repeat or is anything upon me? He said: No."
"471","From Ma'mar, from Hammad, he said: When the madman recovers, he performs ablution as for prayer."
"472","From Hisham, from al-Hasan, he said: When the madman recovers, he bathes."
"473","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man applies depilatory paste, is ablution upon him? He said: Is he not bathing? He said: And he must touch his private part; he is the one saying; he said: I said: If he applies it to his legs due to pain in them while in ablution, does he repeat the ablution? He said: Depilatory paste is not a ritual impurity."
"474","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, that Ibn Umar used to say: Whoever kisses his wife while in ablution repeats the ablution."
"475","From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he was asked about the kiss; he said: Ablution is due from it, and it is part of touching."
"476","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, he said: Ibn Umar would go out to prayer after performing ablution, then meet one of his children and kiss him, then call for water and rinse his mouth, not doing more than that; Ma'mar said: Mamsasa is less than madmada."
"477","From Ma'mar, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abu Ubayda, that Ibn Mas'ud said: A man performs ablution due to direct contact, touching with his hand, and the kiss when he kisses his wife; and he used to say regarding this verse: Or you have touched women; he said: It is squeezing."
"478","From Ibn Uyayna, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, he said: I heard Abu Ubayda ibn Abdullah say: Ibn Mas'ud said: The kiss is part of touching, and ablution is due from it."
"479","From al-Thawri, from Muhill, from Ibrahim, he said: When a man kisses with desire or touches with desire, upon him is ablution."
"480","From al-Thawri, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from al-Sha'bi, he said: When he kisses, upon him is ablution."
"481","From Hisham, from Muhammad, from Ubayda, he said: Mulamasa is with the hand; he said: And ablution is due from it, and tayammum when he finds no water; from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Ubayda, the same; Ma'mar said: And Qatada used to say: Ablution is due to the kiss; I think he mentioned it from Ibn al-Musayyib."
"482","From Ibn Mujahid, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I do not care whether I kissed her or smelled basil."
"483","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, that Ubayd ibn Umayr, Sa'id ibn Jubayr and Ata ibn Abi Rabah differed about mulamasa; Sa'id and Ata said: It is touching and squeezing; Ubayd ibn Umayr said: It is intercourse; then Ibn Abbas came upon them while they were so, and they asked him and informed him of what they said; he said: The two clients erred, and the Arab was correct; it is intercourse, but Allah is modest and uses euphemism."
"484","From Ibn Mujahid, he said: I was told from Mujahid, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I do not care whether I kissed her or smelled basil."
"485","He said: And Ibn Sa'id and Ibn al-Musayyib used to say: Ablution is due to the kiss."
"486","From Ibn Jurayj, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, that Umar ibn al-Khattab went out to prayer and his wife kissed him, so he prayed and did not perform ablution."
"487","From al-Awza'i, he said: Amr ibn Shu'ayb informed me, from a woman he named, that she heard Aisha say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform ablution, and he would go out to prayer and kiss me, then pray without renewing ablution."
"488","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Ma'bad ibn Bunana, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissed me, then prayed without renewing ablution."
"489","From al-Thawri, from Abu Rawq, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss after ablution and not repeat, or she said: Then he would pray."
"490","From Ibn Uyayna, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, that Atika bint Zayd kissed Umar ibn al-Khattab while he was fasting and he did not forbid her; he said: And he intended prayer, then went on and prayed without performing ablution."
"491","From Ma'mar, from Amr ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, he said: There is no ablution due to the kiss."
"492","From Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Karim, that he heard al-Hasan say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said while sitting in the mosque during prayer: Then he grasped Aisha's foot without enjoyment."
"493","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was told that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She is only your basil."
"494","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: If a person vomits or causes himself to vomit, ablution is obligatory upon him, and if he regurgitates, ablution is obligatory upon him."
"495","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: What if a man regurgitates and it reaches his chest or throat but not the mouth? He said: No ablution upon him; I said: What if it reaches the throat but he does not spit it and returns it to his belly? He said: Ablution is obligatory when it reaches the mouth and appears; I said: Do you dislike that a man return it to his belly after it appears in his mouth? He said: Yes, but not as a sin; I find it filthy."
"496","He said: I said to Ata: What if I belch and some food comes out of my throat stuck there not from my stomach, do I perform ablution from it? He said: No; I said: What if I belch and a little comes from the windpipe and food? He said: By my life, I hawk much phlegm, then something comes from my throat and head, and there is no ablution in that except what comes from your belly, from your stomach."
"497","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, he said: When regurgitation reaches the mouth, ablution is obligatory in it; if it is dry felt in the throat, he does not perform ablution from it; from Ma'mar, from Qatada, the same."
"498","Al-Thawri said, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, he said: When regurgitation gushes forth, let him perform ablution."
"499","From Ibn Mujahid, from his father, he said: When little or much of it appears on the tongue, ablution is due in it."
"500","From Ibn al-Taymi, from Layth, from Tawus and Mujahid, they said: There is no ablution due to regurgitation."
"501","From Ma'mar, from a man, from al-Hasan, he said: There is no ablution due to regurgitation."
"502","From Ibn Jurayj, from his father, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Ablution is due to vomiting, and if it is regurgitation that overcomes him, let him perform ablution."
"503","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ya'ish ibn al-Walid, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abu al-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) vomited, broke his fast, was brought water and performed ablution."
"504","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A drop of urine came out? He said: Perform ablution from it; it is impurity."
"505","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata said: Perform ablution due to every impurity: urine, stool, silent wind, loud wind, and every impurity exiting from man."
"506","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was told from Ya'la ibn Sayyaba, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever passes silent or loud wind, let him repeat the ablution."
"507","Ma'mar informed us, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Muslim ibn Salam, from Isa ibn Hittan, from Qays ibn Talq, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you passes silent or loud wind, let him perform ablution, for Allah is not shy of the truth."
"508","From Ma'mar, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, that he heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not accept the prayer of one who causes impurity until he performs ablution; he said: A man from Hadramawt said to him: What is impurity, O Abu Hurayra? He said: Silent or loud wind."
"509","From Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar and al-Awza'i, from Wasil, from Mujahid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) noticed a smell while his Companions were with him, and said: Whoever this wind came from, let him perform ablution; its owner felt shy and did not stand, until he said it thrice and none stood, so al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we all perform ablution?"
"510","From al-Thawri, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you causes impurity in prayer, let him hold his nose, then leave."
"511","Ma'mar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: Iyad ibn Hilal informed me that he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Satan confuses one of you in his prayer saying: You caused impurity, let him say to himself: You lie, until he hears a sound with his ear or finds a smell with his nose; and when one of you prays and does not know whether he added or decreased, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting."
"512","From al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man doubtful in his prayer; he said: He does not leave unless he finds a smell or hears a sound."
"513","From Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah, that Abdullah ibn Muhammad, client of Aslam, told him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man came to him and said to him: It seems to me when I pray that something comes out of my urethra, or wind comes out of me; do I break my prayer? He said: No, that is only from Satan; he enters one's urethra until it seems to him wind comes out; when one of you finds that, let him not break his prayer until he finds wetness, wind or hears a sound."
"514","From al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Qays ibn al-Sakan, he said: Ibn Mas'ud said: Satan hovers around a man in his prayer to cut off his prayer; when he fails, he blows in his rear; when one of you senses, let him not leave until he finds a smell or hears a sound."
"515","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: Satan blows in a man's rear; when one of you senses that, let him not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell."
"516","From al-Thawri, from al-Mughira, from Ibrahim, he said: It is said Satan runs in the urethra and bites in the rear; when one of you senses anything of that, let him not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell."
"517","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: What if I doubt whether I caused impurity? He said: Do not stand for prayer except with certainty."
"518","From Ma'mar, from one who heard al-Hasan, saying: When you doubt about ablution before prayer, perform ablution; when you doubt while in prayer or after prayer, do not repeat that prayer."
"519","From Hushaym, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, he said: When you doubt about ablution before entering prayer, perform ablution; when you doubt while in prayer, proceed."
"520","From al-Thawri, from Mughira ibn Khaythama, who complained to Ibrahim al-Nakha'i: When he doubts about ablution, saying: whispering, you did not wipe your head, you did not wash such; he said: That is from Satan; proceed; al-Thawri said: And it used to be said: When that begins, he repeats; when it becomes frequent upon him, he does not repeat ablution and prayer."
"521","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: Pus and blood are alike."
"522","From Ibn Mujahid, from his father, he said: Perform ablution due to pus, the penis and blood; and he mentioned two traits I did not mention."
"523","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, regarding a head wound on a man, he said: If blood flows, let him perform ablution; if it appears but does not flow, no ablution upon him."
"524","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata said to me: Perform ablution due to every blood that comes out and flows, pus, boil, or a small blister when it comes out and flows; ablution is due in it; he said: And if you pull a tooth and blood flows with it, perform ablution."
"525","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, he said: I asked Ibrahim and Mujahid; he said: I said: I cut my hand and blood appeared but did not flow; Mujahid said: Perform ablution; Ibrahim said: Until it flows."
"526","From Ibn Uyayna, from Ibn Abi Najih, he said: I asked Ata and Mujahid about a wound on a man's hand with blood appearing not flowing; Mujahid said: He performs ablution; Ata said: Until it flows."
"527","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, regarding a man from whom pus and blood exit, he said: He performs ablution due to every blood or pus that flows or drips; from Ma'mar, he said: One who heard al-Hasan informed me, saying the same about blood, and he did not consider pus like blood."
"528","From Ma'mar, from Humayd al-Tawil, he said: I asked Sa'id ibn Jubayr about a pimple on my face; I squeezed it and blood came out and I crumbled it with my finger; he said: There is no ablution in it."
"529","From Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: Pus and blood are alike."
"530","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father and Humayd al-Tawil, they said: Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani told us that he saw Ibn Umar squeeze a pimple between his eyes; something came out and he crumbled it between his fingers, then prayed without performing ablution."
"531","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, he said: I went to wipe with a stone; he said: I know only that Ayyub said: He met me with his nail and wounded my hand; blood came out enough to cover the wound; so I said to Tawus: What do you think, shall I wash it? He said: Wash it if you wish; then he said: I see it only little, so leave it to dry."
"532","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: I insert my finger in my nose and it comes out stained with blood? He said: Do not perform ablution, but wash the blood off you, wash your fingers and blow your nose; he said: And if you insert your finger in your nose while in prayer and blood comes out on your finger, do not leave; wipe your fingers with dust and that suffices you."
"533","From Ma'mar, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, he said: Maymun ibn Mihran informed me, he said: I saw Abu Hurayra insert his finger in his nose; it came out stained with blood, so he crumbled it, then prayed without performing ablution."
"534","From Ma'mar, from Abu al-Zinad, he said: I saw Ibn al-Musayyib insert his fingers in his nose; they came out stained with blood, so he crumbled it, then prayed without performing ablution; he said: And Ma'mar gestured how he crumbled it, placing his thumb on his index finger, then crumbling."
"535","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, regarding fluid exiting a wound, he said: There is nothing in it; he said: I said: Even if there is yellowness in the fluid? They said: No ablution is due to fluid."
"536","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata said: No ablution due to eye tears, nor what flows from the nose."
"537","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, regarding a man spitting blood, he said: If blood predominates, he performs ablution."
"538","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I asked Ata about blood exiting in the mouth; he said: When it flows in the mouth, ablution is due in it; if the gum bleeds in the mouth until it protrudes, perform ablution."
"539","From Ibn Uyayna, from Abu al-Zinad, he said: I saw Ibn al-Musayyib insert all ten fingers in his nose; they came out stained with blood, so he crumbled it, then prayed without performing ablution."
"540","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man hawks blood, is ablution upon him? He said: No; I said: Does he rinse? He said: No, if he wishes."
"541","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: I insert a stick in my mouth and blood comes out on it; he said: Do not rinse."
"542","From al-Thawri, from Uthman ibn al-Aswad, he said: Mujahid spat blood and performed ablution."
"543","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man with chest pain coughing blood, or with chest illness discharging pus, is it impurity? He said: No, and no ablution upon him from what is not food."
"544","From a man, from Muhammad ibn Jabir, from Abu Ishaq, that a man asked Alqama ibn Qays, he said: I spat blood? He said: Rinse and pray."
"545","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: If blood flows from the gum in the mouth, ablution is due in it; if you pull a tooth and blood flows with it until you spit, ablution is due in it; and the gum is the flesh above the teeth."
"546","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: I spat in prayer and blood came out in the spittle; he said: Do not rinse if you wish; religion is easy; it reached me that it used to be said: Be lenient, you will be treated leniently."
"547","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, regarding a man spitting blood, he said: When blood predominates, perform ablution."
"548","From al-Thawri and Ibn Uyayna, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, he said: I saw Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa spit blood, then pray without performing ablution."
"549","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: Ablution is performed due to nosebleed, when it appears and flows, little or much."
"550","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man seized by nosebleed that does not stop, until prayer nearly escapes him; what does he do? He said: He plugs his nostril, stands and prays, even if he fears it enters; I said: Then blood falls in his belly? He said: It does not fall in his belly, and prayer is a must, even if it falls in his belly."
"551","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: When a man nosebleeds without stopping, he plugs his nostril and prays, even fearing it enters his belly let him pray, even if it flows; for Umar prayed while his wound gushed blood."
"552","Ma'mar said: It reached me from Ibn al-Musayyib, he said: When his nosebleed does not stop, he gestures with gestures."
"553","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrima, he said: If it does not stop in prayer, he stuffs it."
"554","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: I sensed blood in my nose while in prayer but it did not exit; do I leave? He said: No; I said: I sensed it in the nostril before prayer and it did not flow; shall I blow my nose? He said: If you wish; and he forbids touching the nose in prayer."
"555","From Ma'mar, from Hisham ibn Urwa, he said: I had boils, so I asked my father about them; he said: If they can be stopped, wash them and perform ablution; if they cannot be stopped, perform ablution and pray; if anything exits, pay no mind, for Umar prayed while his wound gushed blood."
"556","From al-Thawri, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, he said: Sulayman ibn Yasar told me, that al-Miswar ibn Makhrama informed him, he said: I and Ibn Abbas entered upon Umar when he was stabbed; we said: Prayer; he said: There is no share in Islam for one who neglects prayer; so he prayed while his wound gushed blood."
"557","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulayka: Ibn Abbas and al-Miswar ibn Makhrama entered upon Umar when they returned from prayer after he was stabbed, and found he had not prayed Fajr; they said: Prayer; he said: Yes, whoever abandons prayer has no share in Islam; so he performed ablution, then prayed while his wound gushed blood."
"558","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When Umar was stabbed, I and a group of Ansar carried him until we brought him to his house; he remained in one faint until dawn broke; a man said: You will not startle him with anything except prayer; he said: So we said: Prayer, O Commander of the Faithful! He said: He opened his eyes, then said: Did people pray? We said: Yes; he said: There is no share in Islam for one who abandons prayer; so he prayed while his wound gushed blood."
"559","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Kharija ibn Zayd, he said: Zayd grew old until urine dribbled from him; he treated it as he could, and when it overcame him, he performed ablution, then prayed."
"560","From al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr and others, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man complained to him, saying: I am in prayer and it seems to me wetness on my penis; he said: May Allah fight Satan; he touches man's penis in his prayer to show him he caused impurity; when you perform ablution, sprinkle your private part with water; if you find, say: It is from the water; so the man did that and it left."
"561","From Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr; a man asked him, saying: I face hardship from urine; when I say takbir and enter prayer, I find it; Sa'id said: Obey me; do what I command you for fifteen days: Perform ablution, then enter your prayer and do not leave."
"562","From Dawud ibn Qays, he said: I asked Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, saying: I perform ablution and find wetness; he said: When you perform ablution, sprinkle your private part; if it comes to you, say: It is from the water I sprinkled, for he will not leave you until he comes to you and harasses you."
"563","From Ma'mar, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Sufyan ibn al-Hakam or al-Hakam ibn Sufyan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he performed ablution and finished, took a handful of water and sprinkled his private part with it."
"564","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Sufyan ibn al-Hakam or al-Hakam ibn Sufyan al-Thaqafi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he urinated and performed ablution, sprinkled his private part."
"565","From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, he said: Ibn Umar when he performed ablution did not wash the trace of urine, but he would sprinkle."
"566","From al-Thawri, from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah al-Nakha'i, from Abu al-Duha, he said: I saw Ibn Umar perform ablution, then sprinkle until I saw wetness behind him on his clothes."
"567","From Ibn Uyayna, from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah, he said: I heard Muslim ibn Subayh say: I saw Ibn Umar perform ablution, then take a handful of water and pour it between his waist-wrapper and belly upon his private part."
"568","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, that Hudhayfa ibn al-Yaman said: When I perform ablution, then something comes out of me after that, I do not count it as this, or he said: Like this; and he placed his saliva on his finger."
"569","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, that Hudhayfa ibn al-Yaman, Zayd ibn Thabit, al-Hasan and Ata saw no harm in wetness a man finds in prayer, so long as it does not drip."
"570","From Ma'mar, he said: I heard Abd al-Hakam ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwa say: It would afflict me in prayer, and I would find wetness, and it would come out of me in prayer; I would leave several times in an hour and perform ablution; so I asked Ibn al-Musayyib, and he said: Do not leave; he said: I thought he thought it only seemed so to me; he said: I said: It is more than that; it hits my foot, or he said: The ground; he said: Do not leave; when you sense that, meet it with your garment; a brother sitting with him said to me: Do you know what he said to you? He said: Wash your garment when you finish prayer; I did not hear it myself; he said: I did what he said, and soon it left me."
"571","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin that he considered dripping impurity; al-Hasan said it too."
"572","From Ma'mar, he said: A man asked him, saying: I find wetness while in prayer; do I leave? He said: No, until it is a drop; I think he said that day: Is there anyone but finds wetness."
"573","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: I found doubt of semen before Zuhr, and did not look at it until I returned from Maghrib, and found semen at the tip of my penis; he said: Repeat all your prayers; I said: What if I prayed Zuhr, Asr and Maghrib, then returned and found madhiy and had not arranged before or after; he said: Do not repeat it, for perhaps you secreted after you prayed; I said: I had intercourse, then went and found doubt before Zuhr, and did not leave until I returned at night, and found dried madhiy at the tip of the urethra; I supped and did not hasten from my supper, then went to the mosque and prayed Zuhr, Asr and Maghrib; saying: I repeated them, and he saw I was correct in what I repeated."
"574","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Qays said to Ata: What about madhiy, would you wipe it lightly? He said: No, madhiy is stronger than urine; it is washed thoroughly; then he began informing us then; he said: Aish ibn Anas, brother of Sa'd ibn Layth, informed me; he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib, Ammar ibn Yasir and al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad discussed madhiy; Ali said: I am a man who secretes much; ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, for I am shy to ask him due to his daughter's place with me; were it not for his daughter's place I would ask him; Aish said: One of the two men asked, Ammar or al-Miqdad; Qays said: Aish named for me who asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that of the two, but I forgot; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is madhiy; when one of you finds it, let him wash that from himself, then perform ablution, perfecting his ablution, then sprinkle his private part; he said: So I asked Ata about the Prophet's saying, wash that from himself; he said: Where the madhiy is, wash from himself, or his whole penis? He said: Rather where the madhiy is from himself only."
"575","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: What if I find madhiy and wash my penis, do I sprinkle my private part in that? He said: No, it suffices you."
"576","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: I have intercourse with my wife and find madhiy after or at it after intercourse other than intercourse, then I shake my penis, bathe, and find before Zuhr doubt of moisture; I find on my thigh and testicles; shall I look whether I find anything or have I permission not to look? He said: If you were secreting, look; if you were not secreting, do not look."
"577","From Malik, from Abu al-Nadr, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from al-Miqdad, that Ali ordered him to ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man when he approaches his wife and madhiy exits from him, what is upon him? For his daughter is with me and I am shy to ask him; al-Miqdad said: So I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and he said: When one of you finds that, let him sprinkle his private part and perform his ablution for prayer."
"578","From Ma'mar, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Aish ibn Anas, he said: Ali said to al-Miqdad: Ask for me the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man who fondles his wife and speaks to her and secretes; were I not shy and his daughter under me I would ask him; so al-Miqdad asked, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let him wash his penis, perform ablution, then sprinkle his private part."
"579","From Ma'mar and Ibn Jurayj, he said: Hisham ibn Urwa told us, from Urwa, that Ali said: I said to al-Miqdad: Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for were his daughter not under me I would ask him about that: When a man approaches his wife and secretes, without controlling it and without touching her; so al-Miqdad asked, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you secretes without touching her, let him wash his penis and testicles; and Urwa used to say: Let him perform ablution when he intends to pray as his ablution for prayer; from Ma'mar, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, the same."
"580","From al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, that Ali said: I was a man secreting much; I was shy to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I ordered a man and he asked him, and he said: In it is ablution; al-A'mash said: Abu Ya'la told us, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyya, that Ali said: I was shy to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while his daughter was under me, so I ordered al-Miqdad and he asked him, and he said: In it is ablution."
"581","From Ma'mar and Ibn Uyaynah, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, who said: I heard Umar saying: Something like a small pearl comes out of one of us; if one of you finds that, let him wash his penis and perform wudu."
"582","From al-Thawri, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar, concerning madhi: he washes his penis and performs his wudu for prayer."
"583","From al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Sulayman ibn Mushir, from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, that Uthman was asked about madhi and said: That is the dripping; for it ablution is required."
"584","From al-Thawri, from Ziyad ibn Fayyad, who said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr saying concerning madhi: he washes his glans."
"585","From Ibrahim, from Abu Hamzah, freedman of Banu Asad, who said: I asked Ibn Abbas. He said: While I was on my mount between sleep and wakefulness, desire overtook me and something came out of my penis until it filled my thigh and what was around it. He said: Wash your penis and what it touched, then perform your wudu for prayer."
"586","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said concerning madhi, wadi and mani: ghusl is for mani, and wudu is for madhi and wadi; he washes his glans and performs wudu."
"587","From Ma'mar, from one who heard Ikrimah, who said: They are three: madhi, wadi and mani. Madhi is what comes with urine and after it; for it there is washing of the private part and wudu as well. Mani is the gushing fluid in which there is desire and from which the child comes; for it ghusl is required. From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, the like of it."
"588","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: I feel madhi running down my thigh while I am praying, and I do not care about that."
"589","He said: And Sa'id said: From Umar ibn al-Khattab: I feel madhi running down my thigh while I am on the pulpit, and I do not care about that."
"590","From al-Thawri, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: I heard him saying: Even if it flowed upon my thigh I would not leave, meaning madhi."
"591","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Ajlan, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj saying: Umar said while on the pulpit: Something like a pearl, or like a bead, runs down, and I do not care about it."
"592","Abu Sa'id Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad ibn Bishr reported to us, at Makkah, who said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata: A sore on my arm? He said: Do not touch it closely, but let water reach it. I said: What if there is blood and pus around the wound, but it has stuck to the edge of the wound? He said: Follow it with wool or cotton with water on it and wash it. I said: Is there no concession for me not to touch it nor clean it? He said: Do not pray while there is blood on you."
"593","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata: A sore on my arm; what if the wound is open-mouthed? He said: Do not put your hand inside it, but let water reach what is around it."
"594","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata: A man with a broken hand with a bandage tied over it? He said: He wipes the bandage alone and that suffices him. He said: He must touch the bandage; his hand's bandage is in place of his hand; he wipes over the bandage with a wiping, and if he misses part of it there is no harm."
"595","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata: What if there is a bandage over a boil on a man's arm, or a slight sore; does he wipe over the bandage or remove it? He said: If it is slight, I like him to remove the bandages."
"596","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, concerning a broken hand or leg and everything severe, when it is bandaged: Allah is most excusing of the excuse; let him wipe the bandages."
"597","From Ma'mar, from a man, from Ata, and from Ibn Uyaynah, from Malik ibn Mighwal, who said: I asked Ata: Do I wipe over the splints? He said: Yes."
"598","From al-Thawri, from al-Ash'ath, who said: I asked Ibrahim about wiping over the splints, and he said: Wipe over them with a wiping, for Allah is most excusing of the excuse."
"599","Israel ibn Yunus reported to us, from Amr ibn Khalid, from Zayd ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ali, who said: One of my forearms broke, so I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he commanded me to wipe over the splints."
"600","From al-Thawri, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl: I struck a camel of mine and wounded myself, so I asked Sa'id ibn Jubayr, and he said: Wash what is around it, and do not let water touch it."
"601","From Abdullah ibn Muharrar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, the like of it. He said: When the wound is bandaged, wipe around the bandage. From Ma'mar, from a man of the Jazira, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, the like of it."
"602","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata: What if my ear aches and washing it is hard for me? He said: Do not clean it thoroughly, but let water reach it only."
"603","From Ma'mar, who said: Asim ibn Sulayman informed me, who said: We visited Abu al-Aliyah al-Riyahi while he was ill and they performed his wudu for him; when one of his feet remained, he said: Wipe over this one, for it is sick. It had redness on it, and redness is swelling."
"604","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, concerning worms coming out of a person, like pumpkin seeds, who said: There is no wudu for him because of it."
"605","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, concerning worms coming out of a person, who said: There is no wudu in it."
